\h Census
\toc1 Census
\toc2 Census
\toc3 Cen.
\mt1 Census
\mt3 often called
\mt2 Numbers
\is1 Introduction
\ip The English word ‘Numbers’ relates to the census of Israeli fighting men so we have chosen to rename it as \bk ‘Census’\bk*. (Actually, there are \em two\em* censuses described in this document, but the plural form of the word feels less comfortable to pronounce.) Hebrew readers call this document ‘Bemidbar’ which is the fourth word in the Hebrew text, and means ‘In the wilderness’. Some European and other translations call it ‘The fourth book of Mosheh’ (Moses).
\ip This document tells about the descendants of Yisrael (called ‘Israel’ in older translations) for the forty years after their departure from Mt. Sinai, until they arrived at the eastern edge of the land that God has promised to give them. This document is named after the census that Yahweh ordered Mosheh to take before the Israelis had left Mt. Sinai.
\ip Then the Israelis purified themselves and celebrated their second ‘pass-over’ festival after some forty years had passed.
\ip Also at that time, the second census of fighting men was taken, i.e., a generation later at Kadesh-Barnea at Kanaan's southern boundary. But from Kadesh-Barnea, none of them entered the land that Yahweh had promised to give them.
\ip When they were still camped east of the Yarden (Jordan) River, two and a half tribes requested to be given territory on that side of the river, although they sent their fighting men ahead with the other tribes to help them conquer Kanaan.
\ip This ‘Census’ document also records how people were often scared and discouraged as they faced hardship, causing them to sometimes rebel against Yahweh and his chosen servant Mosheh who led them. However, Yahweh's (mostly) patient endurance of their behaviour is told here, and his faithfulness throughout their generations. It reveals Mosheh as an obedient yet humble leader who was devoted both to Yahweh and to the people he had responsibility for.
\iot Main components of this account
\io1 The Israelis prepare to depart from Sinai \ior 1:1–9:23\ior*
\io2 a. The first Israeli census \ior 1:1–4:49\ior*
\io2 b. Various laws and regulations \ior 5:1–8:26\ior*
\io2 c. The second celebration of the messenger's ‘pass-over’ \ior 9:1-23\ior*
\io1 From Mt. Sinai to Moav (Moab)\ior 10:1–21:35\ior*
\io1 The events in Moav \ior 22:1–32:42\ior*
\io1 The places passed through by the Israelis \ior 33:1-49\ior*
\io1 Warnings before crossing the Yarden (Jordan) river \ior 33:50–36:13\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\ie
\c 1
\s1 The first census of the Israelis by Mosheh
\rem /s1 The First Census of Israel; The Census; Israel's First Census; Israel in the wilderness of Sinai
\p
\v 1 In¦61066 April of¦61066 the year¦61073 after¦61075 the Israeli people \add ≈escaped from\add* Egypt¦61077 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add*, Yahweh¦61062 spoke¦61061 to Mosheh¦61065 \add !(Moses¦61065)\add* in the Sinai¦61067 wilderness¦61066 in the \add ≈sacred¦61068\add* tent¦61068, saying¦61078,\x + \xo 1:1-46: \xt Num 26:1-51.\x*
\v 2 “\add ≈Count all the men who are Yisrael's¦61089 descendants by their clans¦61090 and families, being sure to list all their names¦61094\add*.
\v 3 \add Only include those\add* who are twenty¦61101 or older and able \add to be recruited\add* as soldiers. You¦61112 and Aharon¦61113 must¦61109 enrol¦61109 them into military¦61111 divisions¦61111.
\v 4 \add ≈The¦61122 leader of¦61124 each tribe¦61119 will¦61116 accompany\add* you.
\p
\v 5 These¦61127 are¦61128 the names¦61128 of¦61128 the men¦61129 who¦61130 will¦61131 \add ≈assist\add* you:
\li1 Elitsur¦61134 (Shedeyur's¦61137 son¦61135) from Reuven¦61133,
\li1
\v 6 Shelumiel¦61140 (Tsuri-Shaddai's¦61143 son¦61141) from Shimeon \add !(Simeon)\add*,
\li1
\v 7 Nahshon¦61146 (Amminadav's¦61149 son¦61147) from Yehudah \add !(Judah)\add*,
\li1
\v 8 Netanel¦61152 (Tsuar's¦61155 son¦61153) from Yissakar \add !(Issachar)\add*,
\li1
\v 9 Eliav¦61158 (Helon's¦61161 son¦61159) from Zevulun,
\li1
\v 10 Elishama (Ammihud's¦61169 son) from Yosef's¦61164 son Efrayim¦61165,
\li1 Gamliel¦61171 (Pedahtsur's¦61174 son) from Yosef's son Menashsheh¦61170 \add !(Manasseh¦61170)\add*,
\li1
\v 11 Avidan (Gideoni's son¦61178) from Benyamin,
\li1
\v 12 Ahiezer¦61183 (Ammishaddai's¦61186 son¦61184) from Dan,
\li1
\v 13 Pagiel¦61189 (Okran's¦61192 son¦61190) from Asher,
\li1
\v 14 Elyasaf¦61195 (Reuel's¦61198 son¦61196) from Gad,
\li1
\v 15 Ahira¦61201 (Enan's¦61204 son¦61202) from Naftali.
\v 16 They¦61215 were the leaders of their tribes¦61211—chosen out of their communities¦61209, and leaders of \add units of\add* one thousand \add soldiers\add*.
\p
\v 17 Mosheh¦61219 and¦61220 Aharon¦61220 took¦61218 those¦61223 men¦61222 whose names¦61226 had¦61225 been¦61225 \add ≈given\add*
\v 18 and¦61228 they assembled the entire¦61229 community¦61231 that April. \add ≈For each tribe,\add* they recorded¦61236 their¦61248 ancestry¦61241 by¦61242 clan, counting the names¦61243 of those men who were twenty¦61245 or over,
\v 19 just as¦61250 Yahweh¦61252 had¦61251 commanded¦61251 Mosheh¦61255. \add ≈So\add* he¦61251 counted¦61256 them¦61256 \add there\add* in¦61257 the¦61257 Sinai¦61258 wilderness¦61257,
\v 20-21 individually counting those \add in each tribe below\add* by their¦61273 clan, and only including¦61261 males who were¦61261 twenty¦61278 or older and able to fight in battle:
\li1 46,500 men from the tribe of Reuven¦61264,
\li1
\v 22-23 59,300 men from the tribe of Shimeon¦61296 \add !(Simeon¦61296)\add*,
\li1
\v 24-25 45,560 men from the tribe of Gad¦61327,
\li1
\v 26-27 74,600 men from the tribe of Yehudah¦61354 \add !(Judah¦61354)\add*,
\li1
\v 28-29 54,400 men from the tribe of Yissakar¦61380 \add !(Issachar¦61380)\add*,
\li1
\v 30-31 57,400 men from the tribe of Zevulun¦61406,
\li1
\v 32-33 40,500 men from the tribe of Efrayim¦61434,
\li1
\v 34-35 32,200 men from the tribe of Menashsheh¦61459 \add !(Manasseh¦61459)\add*,
\li1
\v 36-37 35,400 men from the tribe of Benyamin¦61484,
\li1
\v 38-39 62,700 men from the tribe of Dan¦61510,
\li1
\v 40-41 41,500 men from the tribe of Asher¦61536,
\li1
\v 42-43 53,400 men from the tribe of Naftali¦61562.
\p
\v 44 Those¦61594 were¦61588 the ones that Mosheh¦61591 and Aharon¦61592 and the twelve Israeli¦61593 leaders¦61593 (one¦61600 from each tribe) listed.
\v 45 They¦61606 were all the \add ≈Israelis¦61609\add* who were counted according to their¦61614 \add ≈ancestry¦61614\add*, being men who were twenty¦61616 or older, and¦61618 \add ≈capable of going¦61621 off to battle\add*—
\v 46 603,550 of them in total¦61626.
\v 47 \add ≈However,\add* the Levites \add ≈weren't listed along with¦61644 the other tribes¦61640\add*
\v 48 \add ≈because\add* Yahweh¦61648 had told Mosheh¦61651,
\v 49 “Don't¦61659 list the Levites \add ≈or count them with the other Israelis¦61667\add*.
\v 50 \add ≈Instead,\add* appoint¦61671 \add *them\add* to manage the tent¦61677 \add ≈where the copy of the agreement is kept\add*, along with all its¦61700 equipment. They must¦61690 serve¦61700 inside it as \add required\add*, and¦61670 they should \add ≈set their tents up around¦61701 it\add*.
\v 51 \add ≈When¦61714 it's time to leave that place\add*, the Levites¦61709 must take¦61707 \add @the tent¦61706\add* down and¦61705 when camp \add ≈is set¦61705 up\add*, they must erect it \add again\add*, \add ≈but¦61705\add* any stranger¦61715 who approaches¦61716 it must be¦61717 \add ≈executed¦61717\add*.
\v 52 \add When\add* the¦61720 \add other\add* \add ≈Israelis¦61720\add* set up camp¦61725, each man¦61726 must¦61719 set up with his army division¦61730 by their¦61730 banner,
\v 53 \add ≈but¦61732\add* the Levites¦61747 will camp there around¦61734 the \add ≈sacred tent¦61735\add* and¦61732 look after it¦61739. \add ≈That way,\add* the Israeli¦61744 community won't¦61737 make \add Yahweh\add* angry.
\v 54 \add ≈So¦61754 the¦61755 Israelis¦61756 did¦61754 everything\add* that¦61758 Yahweh¦61760 had¦61759 instructed¦61759 Mosheh¦61763.
\c 2
\s1 Camp layout by tribe
\rem /s1 The Arrangement of the Tribal Camps; The Arrangement of the Tribes in Camp; The Order of Encampment and Marching; Organization for Israel's Camp
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦61769 told Mosheh¦61772 and¦61773 Aharon¦61775:
\p
\v 2 “The \add ≈Israelis¦61787\add* must camp \add ≈with¦61782 each family joining their¦61784 tribe\add*, \add ≈which will be displaying its\add* banner¦61782. They must camp around¦61789 the \add ≈sacred¦61790 tent¦61790 but\add* at¦61782 a distance¦61788.
\p
\v 3 On¦61796 the eastern¦61796 side facing the sunrise¦61797 will be Yehudah's¦61800 \add !(Judah's¦61800)\add* banner and¦61802 their¦61801 army divisions¦61801, led by Amminadav's¦61808 son¦61806 Nahshon¦61805
\v 4 with 74,600 in his¦61810 division¦61810.
\v 5 The¦61824 tribe¦61820 of Yissakar¦61821 \add !(Issachar¦61821)\add* will \add ≈set up\add* next to them, led by Tsuar's¦61828 son¦61826 Netanel¦61825,
\v 6 with 54,400 in his division¦61830.
\v 7 Then¦61843 the tribe¦61839 of Zevulun¦61840, led by Helon's¦61847 son¦61845 Eliav¦61844,
\v 8 with 57,400 in his division¦61849.
\v 9 The total number in the divisions¦61872 in the Yehudah¦61861 camp¦61860 is 186,400, and \add ≈when travelling\add*, \add ≈they'll¦61874 all go at the front\add*.
\p
\v 10 On¦61884 the southern¦61880 side \add of the sacred tent\add* will be Reuven's¦61879 banner, led by Shedeyur's¦61888 son¦61886 Elitsur¦61885
\v 11 with 46,500 in his division¦61890.
\v 12 The tribe¦61900 of Shimeon¦61901 \add !(Simeon¦61901)\add* will \add ≈set up\add* next to them, led by Tsuri-Shaddai's son¦61906 Shelumiel¦61905
\v 13 with 59,300 in his¦61912 division¦61912.
\v 14 Then¦61920 the tribe¦61920 of Gad¦61921, led by Reuel's¦61928 son¦61926 Elyasaf¦61925.
\v 15 with 45,650 in his¦61930 division¦61930.
\v 16 The total number in the divisions¦61953 in the Reuven¦61943 camp¦61942 is 151,450, and \add ≈when travelling\add*, \add ≈they'll¦61955 all go second¦61954\add*.
\p
\v 17 Then the Levites¦61963 will go next with their¦61974 own banners in¦61964 the order that they were camped, \add carrying\add* the \add ≈sacred¦61959 tent¦61959\add*.
\p
\v 18 On the western side \add of the sacred tent\add* will be Efrayim's¦61979 banner, led by Ammihud's¦61988 son¦61986 Elishama
\v 19 with 40,500 in his¦61990 division¦61990.
\v 20 The¦62002 tribe¦61998 of Menashsheh¦61999 \add !(Manasseh¦61999)\add* will \add ≈set up\add* next to them, led by Pedahtsur's¦62006 son¦62004 Gamliel¦62003
\v 21 with 32,200 in his¦62008 division¦62008.
\v 22 Then¦62015 the tribe¦62015 of Benyamin¦62016 led by Gideoni's son¦62021 Avidan
\v 23 with 35,400 in his¦62025 division¦62025.
\v 24 The total number in the divisions¦62044 in the Efrayim¦62037 camp¦62036 is 108,100, and \add ≈when travelling\add*, \add ≈they'll¦62046 all go third¦62045\add*.
\p
\v 25 On¦62056 the northern¦62052 side \add of the sacred tent\add* will be Dan's¦62051 banner, led by Ammishaddai's¦62060 son¦62058 Ahiezer¦62057
\v 26 with 62,700 in his¦62062 division¦62062.
\v 27 The tribe¦62072 of Ahser will \add ≈set up\add* next to them, led by Okran's¦62080 son¦62078 Pagiel¦62077
\v 28 with 41,500 in his¦62082 division¦62082.
\v 29 Then¦62090 the tribe¦62090 of Naftali¦62091 led by Enan's¦62098 son¦62096 Ahira¦62095
\v 30 with 53,400 in his¦62100 division¦62100.
\v 31 The total number in the divisions in the Dan¦62112 camp¦62111 is 157,600, and \add ≈when travelling\add*, \add ≈they'll¦62121 all go last¦62120\add* with their¦62122 banners.
\p
\v 32 Those¦62129 are the listed \add ≈Israelis¦62127 by their¦62136 ancestral¦62131 tribes\add* \add ≈with a total¦62132 of 603,500 fighting men\add*.
\v 33 However, \add ≈following\add* Yahweh's¦62155 instructions¦62154, the Levites weren't listed among them.
\p
\v 34 \add ≈So¦62160\add* the¦62161 \add ≈Israelis¦62162\add* did everything¦62163 that¦62164 Yahweh¦62167 commanded¦62166 Mosheh¦62170. They¦62173 camped¦62173 under their banners, and \add ≈travelled grouped in their tribes and clans¦62178\add*.
\c 3
\s1 Aharon's sons
\rem /s1 The Levites; The Sons of Aaron; Levites Appointed for Service; Aaron's Sons
\p
\v 1 \add ≈The following\add* are¦62185 the descendants¦62185 of¦62185 Aharon¦62186 \add !(Aaron¦62186)\add* and¦62187 Mosheh as on the day¦62188 when¦62189 Yahweh¦62190 spoke¦62189 with¦62194 Mosheh on Mt¦62194. Sinai¦62195:
\v 2 Aharon's¦62201 sons¦62199 were: Nadav¦62204 (the oldest), Avihu¦62205, Eleazar¦62206, and¦62197 Itamar¦62207.\x + \xo 3:2: \xt Num 26:60.\x*
\v 3 They¦62212 were \add all\add* anointed¦62214 as¦62219 priests¦62219 and \add ≈served¦62219 in that role\add*,
\v 4 \add ≈except that\add* Nadav¦62222 and Avihu¦62223 died¦62221 \add ≈in front¦62224\add* of¦62224 Yahweh¦62225 when¦62226 they offered¦62226 \add ≈unacceptable\add* fire¦62227 to¦62229 \add *him\add* in the¦62231 Sinai¦62232 wilderness¦62231, and \add so\add* they had no sons¦62233. \add ≈So¦62221\add* Eleazar¦62239 and Itamar¦62240 served¦62238 as¦62238 priests¦62238 \add ≈alongside\add* their¦62245 father¦62245 Aharon¦62244.\x + \xo 3:4: \xt Lev 10:1-2; Num 26:61.\x*
\s1 The Levites as ransom for their sons
\rem /s1 The Duties of the Levites; The Levites Are Appointed to Serve the Priests
\p
\v 5 Then Yahweh¦62249 told Mosheh¦62252,
\v 6 “Summon the Levites to come and stand¦62260 in¦62262 front¦62262 of¦62262 Aharon¦62263 the priest¦62264, so they¦62265 can assist¦62265 him¦62266.
\v 7 They¦62268 must¦62268 perform¦62268 duties¦62271 for him¦62271 and for the entire¦62275 community¦62277 at and around the \add ≈sacred¦62285 tent¦62285\add*,
\v 8 including¦62295 looking after all¦62290 of its equipment and¦62295 \add ≈fulfilling the obligations\add* of the \add ≈Israelis¦62299\add*.
\v 9 You¦62318 must¦62306 assign the Levites¦62309 to Aharon¦62310—out of¦62311 all the \add ≈Israelis¦62317\add* it's them who are¦62312 assigned¦62313 \add to serve the priests\add*.
\v 10 Appoint¦62326 Aharon¦62322 and his¦62325 sons¦62325 as priests and to preserve the priesthood¦62330. Any other person \add ≈who tries to act as a priest\add* \add ≈must¦62326 be executed¦62333\add*.”
\p
\v 11 Then Yahweh¦62337 told Mosheh¦62340,
\v 12 “Out of all the \add ≈Israelis¦62350\add*, I've¦62345 taken¦62345 the Levites instead of the \add ≈oldest son from¦62358 every¦62353 family\add*. The¦62358 Levites \add ≈will¦62360 be¦62360 the ransom for those sons¦62358\add*, and¦62360 so they¦62360 belong to¦62361 me¦62361,
\v 13 because¦62364 every firstborn male person and animal is set¦62376 aside as belonging¦62387 to¦62377 me¦62377 ever since I killed those firstborn males in¦62381 Egypt¦62375. I am¦62389 Yahweh¦62389.”
\s1 The census of the Levites
\rem /s1 A Census of the Levites; The Census of the Levites
\p
\v 14 Then in¦62397 the¦62397 Sinai¦62398 wilderness¦62397, Yahweh¦62393 told Mosheh¦62396,
\v 15 “List all the male¦62411 Levites that are at least one month¦62414 old. Count them by their families and¦62415 clans¦62408.”
\v 16 \add ≈So¦62418\add* Mosheh¦62420 listed them¦62419 exactly as¦62425 Yahweh¦62424 had¦62426 commanded¦62426 him to,
\v 17 and these¦62430 were Levi's¦62433 sons¦62431: Gershon¦62435, Kohat¦62436, and Merari¦62437.
\v 18 Gershon's¦62443 sons¦62441 were¦62440: Livni¦62445 and¦62446 Shimei¦62446.
\v 19 Kohat's¦62449 sons¦62448 were¦62451: Amaran¦62451, Yitshar¦62452, Hevron¦62453, and¦62448 Uzziyel¦62454.
\v 20 Merari's¦62457 sons¦62456 were¦62459 Mahli¦62459 and¦62456 Mushi¦62460.
\m Those were the families of¦62463 the Levites¦62464 by their clans.
\p
\v 21 Gershon's descendants were the Livnites and¦62471 the Shimites, so they¦62474 made up the Gershonites.
\v 22 They had 7,500 males that were¦62488 at¦62479 least a month¦62485 old.
\v 23 The Gershonite clans¦62493 were to camp on the western side of the \add ≈sacred¦62496 tent¦62496\add*,
\v 24 and¦62500 \add *their\add* leader¦62500 was¦62505 Lael's¦62508 son¦62506 Elyasaf¦62505.
\v 25 Gershon's¦62513 descendants¦62511 were responsible¦62510 for the \add ≈sacred¦62516 tent¦62516\add*, including¦62517 its¦62518 covering¦62518 and¦62510 the entrance¦62520 curtain,
\v 26 the courtyard curtains, and¦62524 the courtyard entrance¦62529 curtain, that¦62531 surrounded \add *it\add*. Also¦62524 the ropes¦62540 \add ≈used to¦62541 hold them\add*.
\p
\v 27 Kohat's descendants were the Amramites, the Yitsharites, the Hevronites, and¦62544 the Uzziyelites, so they¦62554 made up the Kohatites.
\v 28 They had 8,600 males that were at least a month¦62564 old. They were in charge of the running of the \add ≈sacred¦62572 tent¦62572\add*.
\v 29 The¦62575 Kohatite¦62577 clans¦62574 were to camp of the southern¦62582 side¦62580 of the \add ≈sacred¦62581 tent¦62581\add*,
\v 30 and¦62584 \add *their\add* leader¦62584 was¦62590 Uzziyel's¦62594 son¦62592 Elitsafan¦62590.
\v 31 They were in charge of¦62596 the box¦62597, the table¦62598 and the lampstand¦62599, the altars¦62600 and all the utensils used for ministry, the \add inside\add* curtain and its¦62608 gear.
\p
\v 32 The man who organised the Levites¦62612 was¦62613 Aharon's¦62616 son¦62614, Eleazar¦62613 the priest¦62617. He had oversight¦62618 over all those who were responsible for the \add ≈sacred¦62621 tent¦62621\add*.
\p
\v 33 Merari's descendants were the Mahlites and¦62626 the Mushites, so they¦62629 made up the Merarites.
\v 34 They had 6,200 males that were¦62642 at¦62634 least a month¦62640 old,
\v 35 and¦62646 their leader¦62646 was¦62652 Avihayil's¦62655 son¦62653 Tsuriel¦62652. They¦62651 were to camp on the northern¦62660 side¦62657 of the \add ≈sacred¦62658 tent¦62658\add*.
\v 36 \add *They¦62665\add* were in charge of all the frames¦62666 for the \add ≈sacred¦62667 tent¦62667\add*, its crossbars, posts, bases¦62670, all its containers and¦62662 equipment¦62673,
\v 37 as well as the pillars¦62677 \add used to make\add* the courtyard¦62678 with their bases¦62680, pegs¦62681, and¦62677 ropes¦62682.
\p
\v 38 Mosheh¦62694 and Aharon¦62696 and his sons¦62697 \add ≈set up their tents\add* \add ≈in front¦62685 of\add* \add the entrance on\add* the eastern¦62687 side of the \add ≈sacred¦62700 tent\add*. They were in charge of that tent and \add ?≈the needs of\add* the \add ≈Israelis¦62702\add*. Any stranger¦62704 who approached¦62705 had to¦62701 be¦62706 \add ≈executed¦62706\add*.
\v 39 Mosheh¦62714 and Aharon¦62715 listed 22,000 Levite¦62711 males that were¦62729 at least a month¦62727 old, listing them by their¦62721 clans¦62721 as \add ≈per Yahweh's¦62720 instructions\add*.
\s1 Paying the price for the firstborn sons
\rem /s1 The Redemption of the Firstborn; The Levites Take the Place of the First-Born Sons; Redeeming the Firstborn Sons
\p
\v 40 Then Yahweh¦62735 told Mosheh¦62738, “List all the¦62744 \add other\add* male¦62743 \add ≈Israeli¦62745\add* that are at least one month¦62748 old and \add ≈count them\add*.
\v 41 The¦62758 Levites¦62758 are for me¦62759, Yahweh¦62761, in the place of the firstborn males from every \add ≈Israeli¦62766\add* family, and¦62755 their animals are in place of the \add ≈Israelis'\add* firstborn male animals.”
\v 42 \add ≈So¦62779\add* Mosheh¦62780 listed the¦62790 firstborn¦62789 Israelis¦62790 exactly as¦62781 Yahweh¦62783 had¦62782 commanded¦62782 him¦62784 to.
\v 43 and¦62793 the¦62798 total number¦62798 of firstborn¦62796 males a month¦62802 old or more whose names¦62799 were listed came to¦62804 22,273.
\p
\v 44 Then Yahweh¦62814 spoke¦62813 to¦62815 Mosheh¦62817,
\v 45 “Take the Levites instead of every¦62825 firstborn¦62827 male Israeli¦62828, and the Levites' animals instead of their¦62835 animals, and the Levites will¦62836 be¦62836 mine—I¦62840 am¦62841 Yahweh¦62841.
\v 46 To redeem the 273 firstborn¦62852 Israelis¦62854 who outnumber¦62848 the Levites¦62851,
\v 47 collect¦62856 five silver coins for each one of them. (Use the same silver coins weighing eleven grams, that the priests use in¦62861 the \add ≈sacred¦62862 tent¦62862\add*.)
\v 48 Give¦62868 that \add ≈money¦62869\add* to Aharon¦62870 and¦62871 his sons¦62871 as payment of the ransom¦62872 for those¦62873 excess¦62873 273 males.”
\v 49 \add ≈So¦62876\add* Mosheh¦62877 collected that ransom money¦62879 to¦62883 cover the ransom of the excess¦62882 \add not covered by the number of\add* Levites¦62885.
\v 50 He¦62890 collected 1,365 silver coins from the firstborn¦62888 Israeli¦62889 males (using the standard weight of silver from the sanctuary¦62901)
\v 51 and gave¦62903 \add *it¦62903\add* to¦62909 Aharon¦62909 and his¦62910 sons¦62910 just¦62915 as¦62915 Yahweh¦62914 had¦62916 commanded¦62916.
\c 4
\s1 Kohat's descendants' duties
\rem /s1 The Duties of the Levite Clan of Kohath; Duties of the Kohathite Clan; The Kohathites
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦62924 told Mosheh¦62927 \add !(Moses¦62927)\add* and¦62928 Aharon¦62930 \add !(Aaron¦62930)\add*,
\v 2 “\add ≈Take¦62941 a detailed census\add* of Kohat's¦62938 male descendants by their¦62942 clans¦62942 and families
\v 3 \add ≈who are from twenty-five up to fifty¦62953 years¦62948 old\add* and who goes into the¦62961 \add ≈sacred¦62961 tent¦62961\add* to minister.
\p
\v 4 This is¦62965 what the Kohatites are responsible for concerning the \add ≈sacred¦62971 tent¦62969 including the inner room\add*:
\v 5 When¦62974 \add ≈it's time to break camp¦62978\add*, Aharon¦62975 and his¦62976 sons¦62976 must¦62974 enter and take¦62979 down¦62979 the curtain¦62981 that veils it, and then¦62974 use that to cover¦62983 the box¦62987 \add ≈containing the agreement\add*.
\v 6 Then¦62990 they¦62990 must¦62990 cover it¦62991 with \add ?≈fine\add* leather, followed by a blue cloth, and¦62990 then¦62990 put¦63001 its¦63002 \add carrying\add* poles¦63002 \add through the rings\add*.
\p
\v 7 They must¦63008 spread¦63008 a blue cloth over the \add ≈sacred bread table¦63006\add*, then¦63004 place the dishes¦63018, pans¦63018, bowls¦63021, and¦63004 jugs¦63023 for the drink¦63024 offerings¦63024 on top of¦63023 that, along with the \add ≈sacred\add* bread.
\v 8 Then¦63030 they¦63030 must¦63030 spread¦63030 a scarlet¦63034 cloth over¦63031 all that, and cover¦63035 that again with¦63037 \add ?≈fine\add* leather, and then¦63030 put¦63040 its¦63043 poles¦63043 \add through the rings\add*.
\p
\v 9 They must¦63045 spread a blue cloth over the lampstand¦63052 with¦63072 its \add oil\add* lamps¦63056, its tongs¦63059 and trays¦63062, and the oil containers that¦63068 are used for¦63071 it¦63071.
\v 10 Then¦63074 they¦63074 must¦63074 wrap the lampstand and all its equipment in \add ?≈fine\add* leather, and place it \add all\add* on¦63087 its carrying¦63089 frame¦63089.
\p
\v 11 Then¦63091 the must¦63095 spread¦63095 a blue cloth over the gold¦63094 \add incense\add* altar¦63093, and cover¦63098 that again with¦63100 \add ?≈fine\add* leather, and then¦63091 put¦63103 its¦63106 poles¦63106 \add through the rings\add*.
\v 12 Then¦63108 they must¦63108 get all the \add other\add* utensils that they use in¦63118 the \add ≈sacred¦63119 tent¦63119\add*, and cover¦63125 that again with¦63118 \add ?≈fine\add* leather, and place¦63119 it \add all\add* on¦63118 its carrying¦63133 frame¦63133.
\v 13 They¦63135 need to remove the ashes¦63135 from¦63135 the \add bronze\add* altar¦63138 and¦63139 spread¦63139 a purple¦63142 cloth¦63142 over it¦63140,
\v 14 and put all¦63148 the utensils¦63150 they use on¦63153 top of it: the trays, meat forks¦63160, shovel¦63163 and basins¦63166 for the altar¦63169. Then¦63144 they must¦63144 cover¦63172 it with \add ?≈fine\add* leather, and then¦63144 put its¦63176 poles¦63176 \add through the rings\add*.
\v 15 Aharon¦63179 and his¦63181 sons¦63181 must¦63178 finish¦63178 covering¦63182 the \add ≈sacred tent\add* and all its utensils and equipment when \add ≈they're about¦63181 to move camp¦63193\add*. Then¦63178 the Kohatites can come¦63197 to carry¦63201 it all without touching¦63204 the \add ≈inner room¦63185\add* so¦63196 they won't¦63202 die¦63208. That's the responsibility of Kohat's¦63200 descendants—\add carrying\add* the \add ≈sacred tent\add*.
\p
\v 16 Eleazar¦63218 (son¦63220 of Aharon¦63222 the priest¦63223) is in¦63241 charge¦63217 of the lamp oil and the fragrant¦63227 incense¦63226, the regular¦63229 grain¦63228 offering¦63228, the anointing¦63231 oil, and the oversight¦63232 of the \add ≈sacred¦63241 tent¦63241\add* and the inner room¦63241, including¦63226 everything that's used inside them.
\p
\v 17 Then Yahweh¦63246 told Mosheh¦63249 and¦63250 Aharon¦63252,
\v 18 “Don't¦63255 allow the Kohatite¦63262 Levites¦63264 to \add ≈get wiped out\add* \add by mishandling the most sacred items\add*,
\v 19 \add ≈but¦63266 take these precautions on¦63273 their behalf so\add* they won't¦63271 die¦63272 when¦63273 they approach the \add ≈most sacred¦63276 items\add*: Get Aharon¦63278 and his sons¦63279 to go¦63280 and show \add ≈each of them personally\add* the \add ≈correct and proper way to do¦63268 his duties\add*.
\v 20 \add ≈However,\add* they must¦63294 never \add go early\add* to¦63295 \add ≈set their eyes on\add* the¦63299 \add ≈sacred¦63299 objects¦63299\add*, \add ≈even briefly\add*, or they'll¦63294 die¦63300.”
\s1 Gershon's descendants' duties
