\v 49 Those were the¦63737 ones counted¦63752 by Mosheh \add ≈following Yahweh's¦63738 instructions¦63755\add*. Each man's name was listed by Mosheh, along with¦63741 his duties and what was his responsibility to carry¦63751.
\c 5
\s1 Handling ceremonial ‘uncleanness’
\rem /s1 The Purity of the Camp; Purity in Israel's Camp; Unclean People; Unclean Persons
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦63763 told Mosheh¦63766 \add !(Moses¦63766)\add*,
\v 2 “Order¦63773 the \add ≈Israelis¦63772\add* that¦63774 anyone with a skin¦63780 disease¦63780 or a discharge¦63783, and¦63781 anyone who's¦63783 ‘unclean¦63785’ because¦63786 they¦63774 touched a corpse¦63786, must be sent¦63774 outside the camp¦63777.
\v 3 Whether they're male¦63788 or female¦63791, they must¦63792 be sent outside¦63795 the camp so that¦63803 the whole camp doesn't become ‘unclean¦63799’ \add because\add* I'm¦63804 living¦63805 there \add right\add* amongst¦63806 them.”
\v 4 \add ≈So¦63808 the Israelis¦63811\add* did what Yahweh¦63821 told Mosheh¦63824, and¦63808 sent¦63813 those people¦63811 outside¦63817 the camp¦63818.
\s1 Reparations for crimes
\rem /s1 Confession and Restitution; Restitution for Wrongs; Repayment for Wrongs Done
\p
\v 5 Then Yahweh¦63832 told Mosheh¦63835,
\v 6 “Tell the \add ≈Israelis¦63841\add* that when any man¦63843 or¦63844 a woman¦63846 \add ≈disobeys God by doing any of the things that humans¦63852 do¦63848\add* when they're unfaithful¦63853 towards Yahweh¦63855, then that person is guilty¦63856
\v 7 and¦63860 they must confess¦63860 their¦63863 \add ≈disobedience\add*. Then¦63860 that¦63864 person must make full reparation to whoever they wronged¦63869, along with¦63870 an extra twenty¦63871 percent¦63872 \add of the cost\add*.
\v 8 \add ≈However,\add* if¦63879 reparation to \add ≈the victim isn't¦63881 possible\add* \add for some reason\add*, then¦63879 it must¦63895 be paid to Yahweh¦63889 via a priest¦63890, in addition¦63879 to the ram¦63892 \add that will be offered\add* for that person's¦63882 atonement¦63893.
\v 9 Any¦63908 sacred¦63905 contributions¦63902 by the \add ≈Israelis¦63906\add* that¦63909 are presented to a priest¦63912 will belong¦63914 to him¦63913.
\v 10 Each person's sacred¦63919 contributions will be their own, \add but\add* anything given¦63925 to a priest¦63926 will belong to him¦63919.”
\s1 Testing for an unfaithful wife
\rem /s1 Concerning an Unfaithful Wife; Cases of Wives with Suspicious Husbands; Protecting Marital Faithfulness; The Test for an Unfaithful Wife
\p
\v 11 Then Yahweh¦63932 told Mosheh¦63935,
\v 12 “Tell¦63942 the¦63941 \add ≈Israelis¦63941\add* that if any man's wife¦63950 \add ≈has an affair\add* and¦63951 is unfaithful¦63951 towards him¦63952,
\v 13 when another man¦63956 secretly has¦63966 sex with¦63969 her, then¦63955 she becomes ‘unclean¦63966’, even though there's¦63968 no witness¦63967 against her and¦63955 she wasn't¦63968 caught¦63972.
\v 14 \add ≈If the husband becomes suspicious, whether or¦63985 not¦63997 she's¦63998 actually\add* become ‘unclean¦63998’,
\v 15 then¦64000 \add *he¦64000\add* should take \add *her\add* to¦64005 a priest¦64007. He¦64008 must also bring¦64034 an offering on her behalf: two litres of barley¦64016 flour¦64015. It¦64020 must not¦64022 have any oil¦64021 or \add ≈spices mixed into it\add* because¦64027 it's¦64031 a grain¦64032 offering for suspicion—\add ≈for determining if unfaithfulness has occurred\add*.
\p
\v 16 Then¦64037 the priest¦64039 must¦64037 \add ≈lead her forward\add* and¦64037 stand¦64040 her in¦64041 front¦64041 of¦64041 Yahweh¦64042.
\v 17 He¦64044 must¦64044 \add ≈fill\add* a pottery jar with¦64048 sacred¦64047 water, and¦64044 then¦64044 mix some dust¦64053 from¦64051 the floor¦64056 of¦64056 \add Yahweh's\add* residence into¦64061 the water.
\v 18 Then¦64065 the priest must stand¦64065 the woman¦64069 \add ≈in¦64087 front¦64070\add* of Yahweh¦64071 and¦64065 \add ≈let¦64072 her hair down\add*, then¦64065 he must place the suspicion grain offering on¦64087 her palm. (It's a grain offering for jealousy¦64085.) The priest must be \add ≈holding\add* the water¦64090 of bitterness¦64091 that¦64092 brings¦64092 a curse¦64092
\v 19 and tell the woman¦64100 to make¦64094 this oath: “If¦64101 no \add other\add* man¦64105 \add ≈slept\add* with¦64106 you, and if¦64107 you didn't¦64103 \add ≈dirty yourself while you're married\add*, then¦64094 be¦64114 free¦64114 from¦64115 this water¦64115 of¦64115 bitterness¦64116 that¦64117 brings¦64117 a curse¦64117.
\v 20 \add ≈But¦64120\add* if¦64121 you¦64122 \add ≈have¦64122 cheated on\add* your husband¦64124 and become ‘unclean¦64126’ and slept with some other¦64133 guy, \add there'll be consequences\add*.
\v 21 Then¦64136 the priest¦64137 will make the woman¦64140 take that curse as an oath, and \add *he'll¦64136\add* tell \add *her\add*, “Yahweh will \add ≈make your experience\add* a curse and your people¦64152 \add ≈will see the results of¦64152 the\add* oath, when¦64153 Yahweh gives \add ≈disease to your genitals\add* and makes¦64153 your belly¦64161 swell¦64162.
\v 22 This water¦64165 will¦64164 \add ≈invoke\add* the curse¦64166 to make your belly¦64170 swell¦64169 and¦64164 your \add ≈genitals shrivel\add*.” Then¦64164 the woman¦64174 must¦64164 say¦64173, “Indeed, let it be so.”
\p
\v 23 Then¦64179 the priest¦64184 must¦64179 write¦64179 those¦64183 curses¦64182 on¦64185 a scroll¦64185, then¦64179 wipe¦64186 \add the ink\add* into¦64187 the water¦64189 of¦64189 bitterness¦64190.
\v 24 He must¦64201 make the woman¦64195 drink that water¦64192 of¦64198 bitterness¦64199 that brings¦64200 the curse¦64200, and¦64201 \add *it¦64192\add* will¦64201 enter¦64201 into her¦64202.
\v 25 Then¦64207 he'll¦64214 take the grain¦64212 offering¦64212 of suspicion from her hand¦64209, and hold it up \add ≈in¦64218 front¦64218\add* of Yahweh¦64219, and then¦64207 take it to¦64222 the altar¦64224.
\v 26 \add *He'll\add* take¦64226 some of the grain¦64230 as a memorial¦64233 portion and¦64226 burn¦64234 it on the altar¦64235. Then¦64226 he'll¦64226 make the woman¦64240 drink¦64237 the water¦64243.
\v 27 \add ≈After she's¦64249 drunk¦64245 it\add*, if¦64250 she was ‘unclean¦64252’ and unfaithful¦64253 to her husband¦64255, the water will carry that¦64259 curse into her, and her belly¦64262 will swell¦64261 and her \add ≈genitals will get diseased\add*, and the woman¦64266 will become¦64265 a curse among her people¦64269.
\v 28 \add ≈However,\add* if¦64271 she hadn't defiled herself¦64274 and is¦64276 pure¦64276, then¦64271 she'll¦64278 be free¦64278 and \add be able to\add* \add ≈have¦64274 children\add*.
\p
\v 29 That's the rule about¦64283 jealousy¦64284 when a wife¦64287 \add ≈cheats on\add* her¦64289 husband¦64289 and¦64290 defiles¦64290 herself¦64290,
\v 30 or when a \add ≈husband\add* \add ≈becomes jealous¦64298 and suspicious\add* and he¦64299 stands¦64303 \add ≈his¦64302 wife¦64302\add* \add ≈in¦64307 front¦64307\add* of¦64307 Yahweh¦64308, and the priest¦64311 applies this¦64316 ruling to her¦64310.
\v 31 Then¦64318 \add ≈the husband\add* will be¦64318 \add ≈innocent\add*, and¦64321 that¦64322 women will \add ≈bear¦64323 the consequences\add* of¦64326 her¦64326 wrongdoing.
\c 6
\s1 Instructions for the Nazirite vow
\rem /s1 The Nazirites; The Nazirite; Nazirite Laws; Rules for Nazirites
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦64330 told Mosheh¦64333,
\v 2 “Tell¦64340 the¦64339 \add ≈Israelis¦64339\add* that when any man¦64343 or¦64344 woman¦64346 wants to make¦64348 a solemn vow to separate¦64352 themself to Yahweh¦64353 as a Nazirite¦64351,
\v 3 they must¦64357 keep¦64357 away from wine and strong drink, and \add even\add* vinegar¦64358 made from wine or strong drink, plus¦64356 they mustn't drink grape¦64367 juice¦64366 or eat¦64374 either grapes¦64370 or raisins.\x + \xo 6:3: \xt Luk 1:15.\x*
\v 4 For the entire¦64379 time¦64377 of their separation¦64378, they mustn't eat¦64389 anything coming from a grapevine¦64382, \add ≈not even\add* the seeds¦64384 or the skins.
\p
\v 5 “For the entire time¦64406 of their vow¦64394 to Yahweh¦64410 as a Nazirite¦64409, they mustn't cut their hair—they must¦64399 sacred¦64411 and grow¦64413 their hair long.
\p
\v 6 “For¦64421 the¦64420 entire time¦64420 of¦64420 their separation¦64421 to Yahweh¦64422, they mustn't approach any dead¦64426 body,
\v 7 even if it's their father¦64430 or mother¦64431, or brother¦64432 or sister¦64433. They mustn't defile themselves with¦64438 death, because¦64439 their consecration¦64440 to their god¦64441 is¦64442 on¦64438 their head¦64444.
\v 8 They must remain holy¦64449 to¦64451 Yahweh¦64451 for¦64451 the¦64447 whole time¦64447.
\p
\v 9 “\add ≈However,\add* if someone right next to them suddenly¦64459 died¦64455, that would defile¦64460 their consecrated¦64462 head, and¦64453 after the \add regular\add* seven¦64468 days of purification¦64466, they would have to shave¦64463 their head.
\v 10 Then¦64471 on¦64471 the eighth¦64472 day¦64471, they'd have to take two¦64474 doves or¦64476 young¦64478 pigeons to the priest¦64482 at¦64471 the entrance¦64485 of¦64485 the \add ≈sacred¦64486 tent¦64486\add*,
\v 11 and \add *he\add* would take one for a sin¦64492 offering and the other¦64493 for a burnt¦64494 offering—making¦64495 atonement¦64495 for their transgression with the corpse¦64501. Then¦64489 they would consecrate¦64502 their head¦64505 again that¦64507 day¦64506
\v 12 and¦64509 \add ≈restart\add* their days of separation, as well as bringing¦64515 a one-year old male lamb¦64516 as a guilt¦64520 offering¦64520. (Their¦64510 initial days of separation \add ≈won't count\add* because¦64524 they¦64523 were made ‘unclean¦64525’.)
\p
\v 13 “Now these are the instructions for the Nazirites¦64530: Once their days¦64533 of separation¦64534 are fulfilled, \add someone\add* must¦64535 take them to¦64537 the entrance¦64539 of the \add ≈sacred¦64540 tent¦64540\add*
\v 14 and they will¦64543 present¦64543 their offerings¦64566 to¦64547 Yahweh¦64547—an unblemished, one-year old, male lamb as a burnt¦64554 offering, and an unblemished, one-year old, female lamb as a sin¦64561 offering, plus¦64555 an unblemished ram as a peace¦64566/fellowship¦64566 offering,
\v 15 \add ≈along with\add* a basket¦64568 of flat breads¦64569, flour¦64570 mixed¦64572 with oil, and wafers¦64574 spread with \add olive\add* oil, and their¦64578 grain¦64578 and drink¦64579 offerings¦64578.
\v 16 The¦64582 priest¦64582 must¦64581 present¦64581 all that to¦64583 Yahweh¦64584, and \add ≈handle\add* their sin¦64588 offering and burnt¦64591 offering.
\v 17 The ram¦64595 and the basket¦64601 of flat breads¦64602 will be offered as a peace¦64598 offering¦64598 to Yahweh¦64599, and the priest¦64604 will offer¦64603 their grain and wine offerings¦64598.
\v 18 Then¦64612 the Nazirite¦64613 must shave¦64612 their head¦64619 of separation at the opening to the \add ≈sacred¦64615 tent¦64615\add*, and¦64612 taking¦64621 the hair¦64624, must put it¦64627 on¦64628 the fire¦64630 under¦64633 their peace¦64635 offering¦64635 sacrifice¦64634.
\p
\v 19 “The priest¦64638 will then¦64637 take¦64637 the boiled¦64642 shoulder¦64641 from the ram¦64645, and one flat bread¦64647 roll and one wafer¦64652 from the basket¦64651, and place them on¦64656 the palms¦64658 of that Nazirite¦64659 with their consecrated¦64664 head that's been shaved¦64661.
\v 20 Then the priest will raise them as a raised offering to Yahweh¦64672. Those raised breads and the shoulder \add ≈are now sacred¦64673 and belong to\add* the priest. Then the Nazirite¦64684 can drink¦64683 some wine¦64685.
\p
\v 21 Those are the instructions for the Nazirite¦64689 who¦64690 makes a solemn oath to Yahweh¦64693 for their separation¦64696, \add ≈plus what they're able to give\add*. \add ≈They must¦64691 do¦64707 exactly what they promised\add* as per these instructions.”
\s1 The priests' prayer for blessing
\rem /s1 The Priestly Benediction; The Priestly Blessing
\p
\v 22 Then Yahweh¦64714 told Mosheh¦64717 \add !(Moses¦64717)\add*,
\v 23 “Tell¦64723 Aharon¦64723 \add !(Aaron¦64723)\add* and¦64724 his¦64726 sons¦64726 that when the bless¦64729 the \add ≈Israelis¦64732\add*, this is what they must¦64729 say¦64734:
\q1
\v 24 May¦64738 Yahweh¦64739 bless¦64738 you and¦64740 protect you.
\q1
\v 25 May¦64743 \add ≈Yahweh¦64744 give you prosperity and¦64748 show¦64748 grace toward\add* you.
\q1
\v 26 May¦64752 \add *he¦64751\add* \add ≈watch over\add* you and¦64756 give¦64756 you peace¦64758.
\p
\v 27 “\add ≈In that way,\add* they'll¦64761 put¦64761 my¦64764 name¦64764 on¦64765 the¦64767 \add ≈Israelis¦64767\add*, and¦64769 I¦64769 will¦64770 bless¦64770 them¦64770.”
\c 7
\s1 The leaders' offerings at the altar dedication
\rem /s1 Offerings of the Leaders; The Offerings of the Leaders; Offerings of Dedication; Offerings at the Dedication of the Tabernacle
\p
\v 1 When¦64776 Mosheh¦64776 \add !(Moses¦64776)\add* had finished¦64775 setting¦64777 up¦64777 the \add ≈sacred¦64780 tent¦64780\add*, he¦64781 anointed¦64781 it \add with oil\add* and consecrated¦64783 it and all its furniture¦64789, as well as the altar¦64792 and all its equipment.
\v 2 Then¦64802 Yisrael's¦64804 leaders presented \add <gifts\add*. They were¦64809 the leaders of¦64809 the tribes¦64810 who ruled over¦64813 those who'd been listed \add for duties\add*.
\v 3 They¦64817 brought¦64817 their¦64820 gifts to¦64821 Yahweh's¦64822 \add ≈presence¦64837\add* in¦64821 six¦64823 carts¦64825 \add pulled by\add* twelve bulls. Each cart¦64830 was from two¦64833 leaders¦64834, and¦64817 each of the¦64834 bulls was from one¦64836 leader¦64834.
\v 4 Then¦64842 Yahweh¦64844 told Mosheh¦64847:
\v 5 “\add ≈Accept their gifts because they'll¦64852 be¦64852 useful for the running of¦64856 the sacred¦64857 tent¦64857\add*. \add ≈Distribute them¦64860 appropriately to¦64861 the Levites¦64863, depending on each¦64864 man's duties\add*.”
\v 6 \add ≈So¦64868\add* Mosheh¦64869 took¦64868 the carts¦64872 and the cattle and distributed them¦64877 to¦64878 the Levites¦64880,
\v 7 giving¦64889 two¦64884 carts¦64885 and¦64886 four¦64887 bulls¦64888 to the¦64890 Gershonites¦64891 to help them with their¦64893 assigned duties.
\v 8 Then¦64895 he¦64902 gave¦64902 four¦64897 carts¦64898 and¦64895 eight¦64900 bulls¦64901 to the Merarites¦64904 to help them with¦64907 their¦64906 assigned duties under the supervision of the priest¦64912 (Aharon's¦64911 son¦64909) Itamar¦64908.
\v 9 \add ≈However,\add* the Kohaties weren't given¦64917 any because¦64918 they¦64924 were responsible for carrying¦64924 the very holy¦64921 objects, and¦64914 those had to be carried¦64924 on¦64923 their shoulders¦64923.
\p
\v 10 The day¦64931 that the altar was¦64932 dedicated¦64929 and anointed¦64932, the leaders¦64935 brought¦64934 their¦64938 gifts and presented them at the altar,
\v 11 and¦64942 Yahweh¦64943 told Mosheh¦64946, “\add ≈Each day¦64949\add* \add for the next twelve days\add*, one¦64951 leader¦64950 must¦64953 present his offering¦64956 for the altar¦64958 dedication¦64957.”
\p
\v 12-83 \add ≈These were the¦64962 leaders who¦64962 presented their offerings:\add*
\li1 On the first¦64964 day, Amminadav's¦64971 son Nahshon¦64968 \add on behalf of\add* the tribe of Yehudah¦64973,
\li1 on the second day, Zuar's son Netanel \add on behalf of\add* the tribe of Yissakar,
\li1 on the third day, Helon's son Eliav \add on behalf of\add* the tribe of Zevulun,
\li1 on the fourth day, Shedeyur's son Elitsur \add on behalf of\add* the tribe of Reuven,
\li1 on the fifth day, Tsurishaddai's son Shelumiel \add on behalf of\add* the tribe of Shimeon,
\li1 on the sixth day, Deuel's son Elyasaf \add on behalf of\add* the tribe of Gad,
\li1 on the seventh day, Ammihud's son Elishama \add on behalf of\add* the tribe of Efrayim,
\li1 on the eighth day, Pedahzur's son Gamaliel \add on behalf of\add* the tribe of Menashsheh,
\li1 on the ninth day, Gideoni's son Avidan \add on behalf of\add* the tribe of Benyamin,
\li1 on the tenth day, Ammishaddai's son Ahiezer \add on behalf of\add* the tribe of Dan,
\li1 on the eleventh day, Okran's son Pagiel \add on behalf of\add* the tribe of Asher,
\li1 and on the twelfth day, Enam's son Ahira \add on behalf of\add* the tribe of Naftali.
\p \add ≈Each of the leaders presented the following offerings:\add*
\li1 a silver dish (1.5 kg—\add ≈all weights\add* by the standard temple measurement) and a silver bowl (800g)—both of them full of fine flour mixed with oil as a grain offering,
\li1 a small gold dish (110g) filled with incense,
\li1 a young bull, a ram and a one-year-old male lamb for a burnt offering,
\li1 a male goat for a sin offering,
\li1 two cows, five rams, five male goats, and five one-year-old rams for the peace offering.
\p
\v 84 That was the dedication¦65962 of¦65962 the altar¦65963 in¦65964 the day¦65964 it was anointed¦65965, when Yisrael's¦65969 leaders¦65968 \add presented\add* twelve silver dishes¦65970, twelve silver bowls¦65974, and twelve gold¦65980 pans¦65979.
\v 85 Each silver dish¦65986 weighed 1.5kg (\add ≈all weights\add* by the standard temple measurement) and the silver bowls were 800g. The total¦65992 weight of¦65992 the silver was¦65995 around 27 kg.
\v 86 The gold pans¦66017 that had been filled with¦66012 incense¦66008 weighed 110g and¦66019 their total¦66014 weight came to 1.3kg.
\v 87 For the burnt¦66024 offerings there was¦66025: twelve bulls¦66027, twelve rams¦66028, and¦66038 twelve male one-year-old lambs¦66032 along with their¦66038 grain¦66038 offerings. There were twelve male goats for¦66043 a sin¦66043 offering¦66043.
\v 88 For the peace¦66049 offering¦66049, there were 24 bulls¦66052, 60 rams¦66053, 60 male goats¦66055, 60 male one-year-old lambs¦66057. All of those were part of the dedication¦66063 offerings¦66049 for the altar¦66064 after¦66065 it was anointed¦66066.
\v 89 Then¦66069 Mosheh¦66070 entered the \add ≈sacred tent¦66073\add* to speak¦66075 with¦66069 \add @Yahweh\add*. He¦66077 heard the voice¦66080 speaking¦66081 to him from¦66083 between¦66090 the two¦66091 images of¦66088 winged-creatures that¦66085 were on¦66069 the platform above the sacred box¦66088. That's how \add @Yahweh\add* spoke¦66093 to him.
\c 8
\s1 Lighting the seven lamps
\rem /s1 The Seven Lamps; Setting Up the Lamps; Placing the Lamps; Preparing the Lamps
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦66098 told Mosheh¦66101 \add !(Moses)\add*,\x + \xo 8:1-4: \xt Exo 25:31-40; 37:17-24.\x*
\v 2 “Tell¦66107 Aharon¦66107 \add !(Aaron¦66107)\add* that when¦66110 he \add ≈places\add* the seven¦66120 lamps¦66113 \add on\add* the lampstand¦66118, \add ≈they¦66119 must¦66108 light¦66119 up the area in¦66110 front¦66116 of it\add*.”
\v 3 \add ≈So¦66123\add* Aharon¦66125 did it¦66123 just as Yahweh¦66135 had¦66134 instructed¦66134, setting up the lamps¦66132 on the lampstand¦66130 to face¦66129 forwards.
\v 4 The¦66141 lampstand¦66142 from the¦66142 base¦66147 to¦66145 its¦66147 blossoms¦66150 had been made¦66161 by hammering \add a single sheet\add* of¦66150 gold¦66144, just as Yahweh¦66156 had shown¦66155 Mosheh¦66159.
\s1 The dedication of Levites
\rem /s1 Consecration and Service of the Levites; The Setting Apart of the Levites; The Purification and Dedication of the Levites; The Levites Dedicated
\p
\v 5 Then Yahweh¦66168 told Mosheh¦66171,
\v 6 “\add ≈Out¦66180 of all the Israelis¦66179\add*, take the Levites¦66177 and¦66181 purify¦66181 them¦66182.
\v 7 This is how to make them pure: sprinkle the sin¦66192 offering¦66192 water¦66191 on¦66190 them, then¦66184 they¦66193 must¦66186 shave¦66193 their \add ≈entire¦66197 bodies\add* and wash¦66200 themselves¦66202 and their clothes¦66201.
\v 8 They¦66204 must¦66204 take¦66204 a \add ≈young\add* bull along with its¦66209 grain¦66209 offering of flour¦66210 mixed¦66211 with oil¦66212, plus¦66209 a \add ≈second¦66215 young\add* bull for a sin¦66220 offering.
\v 9 You¦66236 must¦66222 have the Levites¦66225 stand at the front¦66226 of the \add ≈sacred¦66227 tent¦66227\add* and¦66229 summon the rest of the \add ≈Israelis¦66235\add* \add there too\add*.
\v 10 Then¦66238 you¦66238 must present the Levites¦66241 \add ≈in¦66242 front¦66242 of¦66242\add* Yahweh¦66243 and¦66244 the \add ≈Israeli¦66247 men\add* must place their¦66250 hands¦66250 on¦66251 them.
\v 11 \add ≈Out of all the Israelis¦66264,\add* Aharon¦66256 must¦66255 present¦66255 the Levites¦66259 as a raised offering to Yahweh \add ≈so they¦66266 can serve¦66267 Yahweh\add* \add with their assigned duties\add*.
\v 12 Then¦66273 the Levites must place their¦66277 hands¦66277 on¦66278 the bulls' heads, and one¦66284 must be given as a sin¦66285 offering and the other as a burnt¦66289 offering to Yahweh, to make¦66291 the Levites \add ≈innocent in Yahweh's¦66290 eyes\add*.
\p
\v 13 “The Levites¦66299 must¦66296 stand¦66296 in¦66300 front¦66300 of Aharon¦66301 and¦66296 his¦66303 sons¦66303, then¦66296 they can be offered as a raised offering to¦66307 Yahweh¦66307.
\v 14 That's how \add *they'll\add* be¦66316 \add ≈distinguished from¦66313 the¦66314 other Israelis¦66314\add*, and¦66316 then¦66309 \add *they'll\add* belong to¦66317 me¦66317.
\v 15 Then¦66320 the Levites¦66324 will go¦66323 to¦66325 serve¦66325 at the \add ≈sacred¦66328 tent¦66328\add* after¦66320 you've purified¦66330 them and¦66320 presented¦66332 them as a raised offering,
\v 16 because¦66336 they're given to¦66340 me¦66340 by all the¦66342 Israeli¦66342 people¦66342—I've¦66353 taken¦66353 them for myself in¦66344 place¦66344 of their firstborn male sons¦66351,
\v 17 because¦66357 every firstborn Israeli¦66362 male person and¦66365 animal belongs to me. I set¦66373 them apart¦66373 for myself when I killed every \add other\add* firstborn in¦66362 Egypt¦66372,
\v 18 \add ≈so\add* I've¦66386 \add now\add* taken¦66377 the Levites¦66380 instead of the firstborn¦66384 Israeli¦66385 sons¦66385.
\v 19 Then¦66388 I've¦66388 given¦66388 the Levites¦66391 out of all the Israelis, to Aharon¦66394 and his¦66395 sons¦66395 to serve¦66399 \add ≈the whole country\add* by serving¦66402 in the \add ≈sacred tent\add* and making¦66408 \add ≈the Israelis innocent in Yahweh's eyes\add*. That way, a \add ≈deadly disease\add* won't¦66413 strike the Israelis when¦66418 they approach the \add ≈sacred tent\add*.”
\p
\v 20 \add ≈So¦66426\add* Mosheh and Aharon¦66428 and all¦66429 the \add ≈Israelis¦66432\add* did¦66447 to the Levites¦66435 \add just\add* what Yahweh¦66440 had¦66439 instructed¦66439 Mosheh.
\v 21 The¦66453 Levites¦66453 purified¦66452 themselves¦66452 and washed¦66454 their¦66455 clothes¦66455, and Aharon offered them to Yahweh as a raised offering, and Aharon offered a sacrifice to \add ≈make¦66462 them innocent in Yahweh's¦66461 eyes\add*.
\v 22 After¦66467 that, the Levites went¦66470 to do their¦66475 \add assigned\add* duties at¦66476 the \add ≈sacred¦66476 tent¦66476\add* \add ≈working under\add* Aharon¦66479 and¦66480 his¦66481 sons¦66481. \add ≈The¦66490 Israelis did¦66492 exactly what Yahweh¦66484 told¦66483 Mosheh¦66487 to do with¦66476\add* the Levites.
\p
\v 23 Then Yahweh¦66497 told Mosheh¦66500,
\v 24 “These are the instructions for the Levites¦66505: from¦66506 the age of¦66506 twenty-five¦66508, Levite¦66505 men will¦66511 begin serving¦66513 the work¦66513 in¦66514 the \add ≈sacred¦66515 tent¦66515\add*
\v 25 until the age of fifty¦66519 when they must¦66521 retire from that work¦66522.
\v 26 They may then¦66528 assist¦66528 their¦66542 fellow Levites¦66541 with guard¦66534 duties¦66542, but¦66528 they can no longer work¦66536 \add directly\add* with the¦66532 \add ≈sacred¦66532 tent¦66532\add*.”
\c 9
\s1 The ‘pass-over’ celebration
\rem /s1 The Passover; The Passover at Sinai; The Second Passover
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦66546 spoke¦66545 to¦66547 Mosheh¦66549 \add !(Moses¦66549)\add* in the Sinai¦66552 wilderness¦66550, in the first¦66559 month¦66558 of the second¦66554 year¦66553 \add ≈after¦66555 they'd left\add* Egypt¦66557,
\v 2 “The¦66563 \add ≈Israelis¦66565\add* must observe¦66562 ‘pass-over¦66568’ at¦66569 the¦66568 appointed¦66569 time¦66569.
\v 3 You all must¦66580 \add ≈celebrate\add* it on¦66575 the evening¦66578 of the 14th of this month¦66575, \add ≈following all the instructions¦66585 that¦66576 you've all been given previously\add*.”
\v 4 \add ≈So¦66592\add* Mosheh¦66593 \add ≈ordered\add* the \add ≈Israelis¦66596\add* to¦66598 \add ≈prepare\add* the ‘pass-over¦66599’,
\v 5 and¦66601 they¦66601 \add ≈celebrated\add* it in¦66605 the Sinai¦66613 wilderness¦66612 \add ≈starting\add* on¦66605 the evening¦66611 of the 14th of that first¦66605 month¦66609, \add ≈following all the instructions¦66616 that Yahweh¦66617 had¦66616 given\add* Mosheh¦66620.
\p
\v 6 \add ≈However,\add* there were some men who¦66628 were ‘unclean¦66630’ (because they'd touched a dead body) and hence they weren't able¦66635 to¦66636 \add ≈celebrate\add* the ‘pass-over¦66638’ that day, \add ≈so\add* they \add ≈approached\add* Mosheh¦66643 and Aharon¦66645
\v 7 and¦66649 \add ≈asked\add* them, “We¦66668 were ‘unclean¦66654’ because we'd touched a dead body, \add but\add* \add ≈how come we're¦66653 excluded\add* from presenting an offering¦66663 to Yahweh¦66664 \add ≈along with¦66665 the other Israelis¦66667\add*?”
\p
\v 8 “\add ≈Wait here\add*,” Mosheh¦66672 \add ≈answered\add*, “and¦66670 I'll \add ask\add* Yahweh¦66678 \add ≈what he¦66677 wants you all to do\add*.”
\p
\v 9 Then Yahweh¦66683 told Mosheh¦66686,
\v 10 “Tell¦66693 the¦66692 \add ≈Israelis¦66692 that\add* for this and¦66711 future generations¦66710, if a person is ‘unclean¦66701’ or \add ≈far from home\add*, then they can \add still\add* \add ≈observe¦66711\add* Yahweh's¦66713 ‘pass-over¦66712’.
\v 11 They can \add ≈start\add* it on¦66717 the evening¦66721 of the 14th of the \em second¦66716\em* month¦66715, and eat¦66728 it \add as usual\add* with¦66717 flat bread¦66726 and bitter¦66727 herbs¦66727.
\v 12 They¦66732 must not break¦66739 \add ≈any of the lambs bones\add*, must not leave¦66732 any of it until¦66734 the morning¦66736, and¦66737 must observe¦66746 it \add ≈following all the normal instructions\add*.\x + \xo 9:12: \xt Exo 12:46; Yhn 19:36.\x*
\v 13 \add ≈However¦66768,\add* any person¦66749 who isn't¦66755 ‘unclean’ or far away, but¦66749 yet who didn't¦66755 celebrate the ‘pass-over¦66760’ \add ≈that first month\add*, must¦66761 be \add ≈driven out of¦66764 the community\add* and¦66749 will¦66773 have to bear¦66773 their \add own\add* sin¦66772.
\p
\v 14 If¦66784 an \add ≈outsider is living among¦66780 you\add* and¦66777 \add ≈celebrates\add* the ‘pass-over¦66783’, they must¦66779 also do it according¦66785 to \add ≈all the same instructions\add*—\add ≈there's only one way to do it whether it's\add* you all, or a foreigner, or a native¦66795 of¦66795 the land¦66796.
\rem /s1 The journey from Sinai to Edom; The Cloud Above the Tabernacle; The Fiery Cloud; The Cloud and the Fire
\rem /r (Exodus 40.34-38)
\p
\v 15 \add ≈When the sacred tent was dedicated\add*, the cloud¦66805 covered¦66804 the \add ≈inner room of the tent\add*, and¦66811 \add ≈every evening¦66811 it¦66812 would look like¦66816 fire¦66818 above\add* the residence, until¦66819 morning¦66821 \add came\add*.
\v 16 \add ≈It remained like that\add* continually¦66825—the cloud¦66826 would cover¦66827 it \add during the day\add*, and¦66828 then at night¦66831, it \add ≈would appear¦66828 like\add* fire¦66830.
\v 17 \add ≈Whenever\add* the cloud \add ≈would be lifted up\add* from¦66836 the tent¦66837, \add ≈then¦66833 the Israelis\add* would \add ≈leave that place¦66844\add*. \add Then\add* wherever¦66845 the cloud settled¦66846 down, \add ≈that's where the Israelis would set¦66841 up camp\add*,
\v 18 \add so in that way,\add* the \add ≈Israelis¦66861 would leave a place whenever Yahweh¦66858 told them, and¦66862 would set¦66859 up camp whenever he told them\add*. As¦66865 long as the cloud¦66872 stayed above the residence, they would \add stay\add* camped \add in that place\add*.
\v 19 Whenever¦66888 the cloud¦66879 remained above the residence for a \add ≈long¦66878 time¦66883\add*, then¦66878 the \add ≈Israelis¦66886\add* would \add ≈follow\add* Yahweh's¦66892 \add ≈guidance\add* and¦66878 wouldn't \add ≈pack up camp\add*.
\v 20 Sometimes¦66913 the cloud¦66899 would only remain above the residence for a few days¦66900, in which case they'd \add ≈leave where they'd just camped, and¦66910 move on as Yahweh¦66908 commanded\add*.
\v 21 If the cloud was lifted up the next morning¦66926, then they'd \add ≈move on\add*—\add in fact\add* whether day¦66932 or¦66931 night¦66933 if the cloud was lifted up, then they would \add ≈move on\add*.
\v 22 Whether it was two¦66940 days¦66940 or a month¦66943 or \add ≈a year\add* that the cloud¦66948 stayed¦66952 above the residence, then the \add ≈Israeli¦66957\add* camp would remain in¦66947 that place, until \add eventually\add* \add ≈moving on¦66947\add* when¦66960 it was lifted¦66960 up¦66960 \add again\add*.
\v 23 \add In that way,\add* \add ≈when Yahweh ordered them to camp, they would, and¦66968 when order to move on¦66982, they'd do that\add*—thus they \add ≈obeyed\add* Yahweh's¦66966 \add ≈instructions to\add* Mosheh¦66984.
\c 10
\s1 The silver trumpets
\rem /s1 The Silver Trumpets
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦66988 told Mosheh¦66991 \add !(Moses¦66991)\add*,
\v 2 “Make¦67000 two¦66996 hammered¦66999 silver¦66998 trumpets¦66997 for yourself¦67003 to use for \add ≈assembling the community¦67005\add* and¦67006 for \add signalling when it's time\add* to leave the camp.
\v 3 \add ≈When¦67011 both are sounded, the whole¦67015 community¦67017 is to assemble¦67013 in¦67012 front of¦67015\add* you¦67014 at¦67012 the entrance¦67020 to the \add ≈sacred¦67021 tent¦67021\add*.
\v 4 \add ≈If¦67033 just one¦67026 is sounded,\add* then¦67024 it's \add only\add* the leaders¦67030 and¦67028 heads¦67031 of clans who must¦67027 assemble¦67028.
\v 5 A \add ≈single blast¦67035\add* means that¦67039 the camps¦67038 on¦67040 the eastern¦67040 side should \add start\add* moving out.
\v 6 A \add ≈double blast¦67042\add* means that¦67047 the camps¦67046 on the southern¦67048 side should \add start\add* moving out. \add ≈So¦67042 the blasts will signal them to get going\add*.
\v 7 (To assemble¦67056 the¦67056 community \add as above\add*, \add ≈use long blows, not¦67058 short blasts¦67057\add*.)
\v 8 The priests¦67063 (Aharon's¦67062 descendants) must¦67064 be the ones to blow the trumpets¦67065. That is a \add ≈permanent¦67069\add* regulation¦67068.
\p
\v 9 When¦67072 you \add ≈need to defend yourselves against an attacker¦67080\add*, then¦67072 you must¦67074 sound¦67082 an alarm¦67082 with¦67076 the trumpets¦67083, and you'll all be \add ≈noticed\add* by Yahweh¦67087, and you'll be saved¦67089 from¦67090 your¦67076 enemies¦67090.
\p
\v 10 On¦67092 festival days and at times of celebrations and at the beginning¦67095 of each new month¦67096, then¦67092 the trumpets¦67098 will¦67097 be blown as the burnt¦67100 offerings and peace¦67103 offerings are made as a memorial¦67106 for¦67105 you all towards your god. I¦67109 am¦67110 your god, Yahweh¦67110.
\s1 The Israelis leave Sinai
\rem /s1 The Israelites Leave Sinai; Departure from Sinai; The Israelites Break Camp
\p
\v 11 Then on¦67115 the 20th of the second month¦67120 in¦67115 that second year¦67115 \add (after leaving Egypt)\add*, the cloud¦67122 was¦67121 lifted up¦67121 from¦67123 above the \add ≈sacred¦67124 tent¦67124\add*
\v 12 and¦67127 the \add ≈Israelis¦67130\add* \add ≈started moving out from¦67132 the Sinai¦67133 wilderness as per the pre-arranged order\add*. The cloud¦67135 moved to the Paran¦67137 wilderness.
\v 13 That was the first¦67140 time that they¦67139 had moved \add ≈as a result of Yahweh¦67144 signalling Mosheh¦67147\add* \add by means of the cloud\add*.
\p
\v 14 Yehudah¦67154 tribe¦67152 with¦67155 their¦67156 banner \add ≈was the first¦67155 to¦67156 leave under the leadership of¦67161\add* Amminadav's¦67163 son¦67161 Nahshon¦67160.
\v 15 Tsuar's¦67174 son¦67172 Netanel¦67171 led the company from Yissakar¦67170 tribe¦67168,
\v 16 and¦67176 Helon's¦67185 son¦67183 Eliav¦67182 led the company from Zevulun¦67181 tribe¦67179.
\p
\v 17 Then¦67187 the \add ≈sacred tent\add* was disassembled, and the men of Gershon¦67192 and Merari¦67194 set¦67189 off, carrying¦67195 the tent.
\p
\v 18 Reuven¦67202 tribe with their¦67203 banner \add ≈was next to leave under the¦67208 leadership of¦67208\add* Shedeyur's¦67210 son¦67208 Elitsur¦67207.
\v 19 Tsurishaddai's¦67221 son¦67219 Shelumiel¦67218 led the company from Shimeon¦67217 tribe¦67215.
\v 20 Deuel's¦67234 son¦67232 Elyasaf¦67231 led the company from Gad¦67230 tribe¦67227.
\p
\v 21 Then¦67236 the \add ≈sacred utensils\add* were carried¦67238 out¦67236 by the Kohatite¦67237 \add men\add*, who¦67238 \add ≈then¦67236 helped set¦67240 up¦67240 the sacred tent¦67243 when they¦67246 arrived¦67246\add*.
\p
\v 22 Efrayim¦67254 tribe¦67252 with their¦67255 banner \add ≈was next to leave under the¦67260 leadership of¦67260\add* Ammihud's¦67262 son¦67260 Elishama¦67259.
\v 23 Pedahtsur's¦67273 son¦67271 Gamaliel¦67270 led the company from Menashsheh¦67269 tribe¦67267.
\v 24 Gideoni's son¦67284 Avidan led the company from Benyamin¦67282 tribe¦67280.
\p
\v 25 Dan¦67294 tribe with their¦67299 banner \add ≈was last to¦67296 leave as the rear guard under the leadership of¦67304\add* Ammishaddai's¦67306 son¦67304 Ahiezer¦67303.
\v 26 Okran's¦67318 son¦67316 Pagiel¦67315 led the company from Asher¦67314 tribe¦67312.
\v 27 Eynan's¦67329 son¦67327 Ahira¦67326 led the company from Naftali¦67325 tribe¦67323.
\v 28 That¦67335 was \add ≈the order of the departures of the companies of the Israeli¦67333 tribes when they¦67337\add* set¦67337 off.
\p
\v 29 Then Mosheh told Hovav¦67342 (son¦67343 of¦67343 the Midianite Reuel¦67345 who was Mosheh's¦67341 father-in-law¦67347), “We're heading towards the place¦67354 that¦67355 Yahweh said¦67356 he'd give¦67359 us. Come¦67361 \add ≈and join us, and we'll¦67363 look after you, because¦67365 Yahweh has¦67368 promised to¦67364 look after\add* Yisrael¦67373.”
\p
\v 30 “\add Thank you but\add* \add ≈no\add*,” Hovav \add ≈replied\add*, “I'll¦67378 \add ≈return\add* to my land¦67384 and¦67375 to my relatives¦67387.”
\p
\v 31 “Please¦67393 don't¦67391 leave¦67394 us¦67395,” Mosheh \add ≈insisted\add*, “because¦67396 you're \add the one who\add* knows¦67401 about camping in¦67403 the wilderness¦67403, and¦67390 you \add ≈could be our¦67402 guide\add*.
\v 32 When¦67408 you come with¦67412 us, Yahweh¦67419 \add ≈will¦67418 be blessing us so we'll¦67421 also bless\add* you.”
\rem /s1 The People Set Out
\p
\v 33 Then¦67424 they¦67424 \add ≈left¦67424\add* Yahweh's mountain \add ≈and¦67424 travelled for\add* three¦67428 days¦67429, with the box¦67430 \add ≈containing\add* Yahweh's agreement¦67431 \add ≈being carried at the front¦67435\add* to find a resting¦67441 place¦67441 for them¦67440,
\v 34 and¦67443 Yahweh's¦67444 cloud¦67443 was¦67445 over¦67445 them¦67445 \add each\add* day¦67446 as they set out¦67447 from¦67448 their¦67447 stop.
\p
\v 35 \add ≈As the box¦67457 started moving\add*, Mosheh¦67459 would say¦67458, “Yahweh¦67462, take action and then your enemies¦67464 will scatter¦67463, and the ones hating¦67466 you¦67466 will flee¦67465 away from¦67467 your \add ≈presence¦67467\add*.”\x + \xo 10:35: \xt Psa 68:1.\x*
\v 36 Then¦67469 \add at the end of the day\add* when¦67469 it¦67469 came to rest, he¦67470 would say¦67470, “Yahweh¦67472, return¦67471 \add to\add* the \add ≈tens of thousands¦67473 of Israelis¦67474\add*.”
\c 11
\s1 Complaints and fire from Yahweh
\rem /s1 The People Complain to Moses; The Place Named Taberah; Fire From the Lord; Complaining in the Desert
\p
\v 1 \add ≈One day,\add* the people¦67481 were complaining¦67482 \add about their situation\add* and¦67486 \add ≈when Yahweh¦67485 heard them¦67492, it¦67495 made him angry\add* \add ≈so he¦67486 sent a fire¦67493 that burnt¦67490 up the edges of¦67496 their camp¦67497\add*.
\v 2 The¦67505 people¦67500 cried¦67499 out¦67499 to Mosheh¦67503 \add for help\add*, and \add *he¦67504\add* prayed¦67504 to Yahweh¦67508, and the¦67510 fire¦67510 stopped,
\v 3 and¦67512 they named that¦67516 place¦67515 Taverah¦67517 \add (which means ‘burning’)\add* because¦67518 Yahweh's¦67523 fire¦67522 had¦67520 burnt¦67520 among¦67521 them¦67521.
\s1 The choosing of seventy elders
\rem /s1 Quail From the Lord; Moses Chooses Seventy Leaders
\p
\v 4 \add ≈However\add*, there was¦67527 a \add ≈group of¦67527 stirrers among the people¦67533\add* that¦67526 \add ≈badly wanted to have meat and other foods to eat\add*. \add ?≈That spread to all the Israelis¦67533 who wept¦67531 and asked\add*, “Who'll give us¦67537 meat to eat?
\v 5 We remember¦67540 the fish¦67543 that¦67544 we¦67546 ate¦67546 in¦67547 Egypt¦67547 for free, \add as well as\add* the cucumbers¦67550, melons¦67552, leeks¦67555, onions¦67558, and¦67559 garlic¦67561,
\v 6 \add ≈but¦67563\add* now¦67563 our¦67564 appetite¦67564 \add ≈has shrivelled up because we don't¦67566 see anything¦67567 to¦67569 eat except¦67568 this ‘stuff’\add*.”
\p
\v 7 (The¦67574 ‘stuff’ \add they ate every day\add* was \add a bit\add* like coriander¦67577 seed¦67575 \add except kind of clear\add*.\x + \xo 11:7-8: \xt Exo 16:31.\x*
\v 8 \add Each morning\add* the¦67584 people¦67584 went¦67583 around gathering¦67585 it, then ground¦67586 it with a \add stone\add* mill or¦67588 pounded¦67589 it in¦67587 a mortar¦67590, then they boiled¦67591 it and¦67596 made¦67593 \add ≈something like bread¦67595 rolls with\add* it. They tasted¦67597 like fresh \add olive\add* oil¦67600.
\v 9 The ‘stuff’ actually descended on¦67602 the camp¦67606 during the night¦67607 with¦67602 the dew.)\x + \xo 11:9: \xt Exo 16:13-15.\x*
\p
\v 10 Mosheh¦67613 heard the people¦67616 weeping¦67617 in¦67627 their tents¦67621 (set up by tribe and clan). \add *He¦67628\add* thought it was wrong, and \add it made\add* Yahweh¦67625 \add ≈very angry\add*.
\v 11 \add ≈So¦67631\add* Mosheh¦67632 \add ≈asked\add* Yahweh¦67635, “Why \add ≈have¦67637 you caused me, your servant¦67638, to¦67645 be in¦67644 trouble\add* \add like this\add*? \add ≈Don't¦67640 you approve of me?\add*. \add ≈Why\add* has the¦67648 burden¦67648 of all¦67649 this people¦67651 group \add landed\add* on¦67644 me?
\v 12 \add ≈Was it me who\add* conceived¦67656 \add *it\add*? \add ≈Did I carry¦67670 it to the land promised to their ancestors¦67682, like I was a wet-nurse\add*?
\v 13 All these people¦67690 come to me to ask me to give¦67697 them meat to eat¦67701. Where would I get \add enough\add* meat \add to feed all\add* them?
\v 14 I¦67705 can't bear \add the load of\add* this¦67714 entire¦67711 people¦67713 group by myself¦67707—it's¦67716 too¦67716 heavy¦67716 for¦67717 me¦67717.
\v 15 If¦67719 that's what you're¦67723 doing¦67725 to me, please¦67728 kill¦67727 me now if¦67730 I've¦67732 found¦67732 favour¦67733 in¦67734 your¦67734 eyes¦67734. \add ≈Then¦67719 I wouldn't have¦67732 to suffer like this\add*.”
\rem /s1 Moses Chooses Seventy Leaders; The Seventy Elders
\p
\v 16 Then Yahweh¦67742 told Mosheh¦67745, “Bring me¦67748 seventy¦67749 of Yisrael's¦67752 elders who you know¦67754 \add ≈are¦67758 good leaders\add*, and take them to¦67763 the¦67765 \add ≈sacred¦67765 tent¦67765\add*, and \add ≈let them take their positions\add* there¦67768 with¦67769 you.
\v 17 I'll come¦67771 down¦67771 and talk with you there¦67774, and I'll take¦67775 some¦67776 of the spirit¦67778 that's on you and put¦67781 \add <it\add* on them¦67782, and then¦67771 they'll¦67783 carry the burden¦67785 of the people¦67786 along with you. Then¦67771 you won't¦67787 \add have to\add* carry \add <it\add* by yourself¦67791.
\v 18 \add ≈Also¦67793,\add* tell the¦67795 people¦67795 that because they wept¦67802 in my hearing¦67803 about¦67803 not having¦67802 meat to eat like you all did in Egypt¦67813, they must¦67796 \add ≈purify\add* themselves for tomorrow¦67798, because I'll provide meat for you all to eat.
\v 19 You won't¦67824 \add just\add* have meat for a day¦67821 or two¦67825, or for five¦67828, ten¦67831, or twenty¦67834 days¦67835,
\v 20 you have it for a \add whole\add* month¦67839 until¦67841 it comes out¦67844 your nostrils¦67845. \add Yes,\add* it'll¦67844 make you all nauseous because¦67849 you rejected¦67852 Yahweh¦67855 who's¦67856 among you, and¦67846 you all wept¦67858 \add ≈in¦67857 front¦67859 of¦67857 him¦67859, complaining\add*, ‘Why did¦67863 we¦67863 ever leave Egypt¦67864?’ ”
\p
\v 21 Mosheh¦67867 \add ≈queried\add*, “There's 600,000 \add ≈able to serve in¦67876 the¦67873 army\add* \add plus women and children\add*, yet you say that¦67874 you'll give¦67880 them \add all\add* enough meat¦67879 to eat¦67882 \add every\add* day for¦67881 month¦67883!
\v 22 \add ≈Even if we killed all the cattle and sheep, or¦67892 caught all the fish in the sea¦67898, that wouldn't be¦67899 enough meat\add* for \add all\add* them.”
\p
\v 23 “\add Do you think that\add* Yahweh's¦67906 \add ≈powerless¦67910\add*?” Yahweh \add ≈replied\add*. “\add ≈Soon\add* you'll¦67914 see¦67914 whether¦67915 or¦67917 not¦67919 my statement will \add ≈come¦67915 true\add*.”
