\p
\v 31 Then¦68044 Yahweh¦68048 sent a wind that blew quails¦68050 from the ocean, and¦68044 \add ≈they dropped\add* on the ground a day's walk in every direction around¦68064 the camp¦68065 \add until they were piled\add* a metre high.
\v 32 \add ≈So¦68072\add* the people¦68073 went out and collected the quail¦68088—\add ≈each¦68081 family getting at least¦68089 the equivalent of¦68083 ten¦68091 large barrels full\add*, and they¦68085 spread the meat around¦68096 the camp¦68097 \add to sun dry\add*.
\v 33 Then¦68110 when they started to \add cook and\add* eat \add some of the fresh\add* meat¦68099, Yahweh¦68106 \add ≈got very angry\add* and struck¦68109 the people with¦68108 a terrible \add ≈deadly disease\add* before they could even chew it.
\v 34 \add ≈So¦68116\add* that place¦68121 was named Kivrot-Hattaavah¦68124 \add (which means ‘Graves of the cravers’)\add*, because¦68125 that was where they¦68128 buried¦68128 the people¦68131 who¦68132 had craved¦68132 \add <meat\add*.
\v 35 From Kivrot-Hattaavah, the¦68137 people¦68137 \add ≈moved on¦68140\add* to Hatserot¦68138 and¦68139 \add ≈stayed\add* \add *there\add*.
