\p
\v 1 \add ≈One day,\add* Miryam¦68144 and Aharon¦68145 spoke¦68143 out against¦68146 Mosheh¦68146 because¦68154 he'd taken¦68153 an \add Ethiopian\add* woman¦68156 (Kushitess) as a wife,
\v 2 and¦68160 they \add ≈challenged\add*, “Did Yahweh really only speak through Mosheh¦68164? Doesn't he¦68165 also¦68168 speak through us¦68170?” Yahweh heard \add what they said\add*.
\v 3 (Now Mosheh¦68176 was¦68177 \add actually\add* a very humble man¦68175—more humble than anyone else \add ≈alive\add*.)
\p
\v 4 Then Yahweh¦68190 suddenly¦68191 told Mosheh¦68194, Aharon¦68197, and¦68198 Miryam¦68200, “Go out¦68201, the three of you, to¦68203 the \add ≈sacred¦68205\add* tent¦68205.” \add ≈So\add* the three of them¦68208 went¦68207 there.
\v 5 and Yahweh¦68211 descended¦68210 in¦68212 a pillar¦68212 of cloud¦68213 and stood¦68214 at¦68212 the tent¦68216 opening and called¦68217 Aharon¦68218 and Miryam¦68219, and the two of them¦68221 \add ≈stepped forward\add*,
