\v 9 \add ≈So¦68272\add* Yahweh¦68275 \add ≈was angry\add* at¦68276 \add @Miryam and¦68277 Aharon\add*. Then¦68272 he¦68277 departed¦68277
\v 10 and¦68279 the cloud¦68279 \add ≈moved\add* from¦68281 the tent¦68282. Then¦68279 wow, Miryam¦68284 had leprosy—her skin had gone as white as snow¦68286. As Aharon¦68288 turned¦68287 to her, he saw, wow, she was leprous¦68293,
\v 11 and \add *he¦68295\add* \add ≈begged\add* Mosheh¦68299, “Please¦68296, my¦68301 master¦68301, please¦68304 don't¦68302 \add ≈make us¦68306 suffer for our foolish¦68309 disrespect and disobedience\add*.
\v 12 \add ≈Don't let¦68316 her¦68316 be¦68316 like¦68317 a still-born baby that's already starting to decompose when its mother¦68321 gives birth to it¦68322\add*.
