\v 13 \add ≈So¦68326\add* Mosheh¦68327 \add ≈pleaded with\add* Yahweh¦68330, “God¦68332, please, please heal¦68334 her¦68336!”
\p
\v 14 “\add ≈If\add* her father¦68344 had¦68346 spit¦68345 in her face¦68347, wouldn't she \add ≈stay inside in disgrace\add* for seven days?” Yahweh¦68340 \add ≈replied\add*. “\add So\add* she must¦68349 be¦68352 put¦68349 outside¦68355 the camp¦68356 for seven days, then after¦68357 that, she \add ≈can enter again\add*.”\x + \xo 12:14: \xt Num 5:2-3.\x*
\v 15 \add ≈So¦68360\add* Miryam¦68361 was sent outside¦68362 the camp¦68363 for seven¦68364 days¦68365, and¦68366 the people¦68366 didn't¦68367 \add ≈move on\add* until¦68369 after she¦68360 \add was allowed\add* \add ≈to return\add*.
\v 16 After¦68374 that, the people¦68376 left¦68375 Hatserot¦68377 and¦68378 set¦68375 up camp in¦68379 the Paran¦68380 wilderness¦68379.
