\v 21 \add ≈So¦68625\add* \add @the twelve men\add* went¦68625 and¦68625 explored the region from¦68630 the Tsin¦68632 wilderness¦68630 \add in the south, all the way\add* up to¦68633 Rehob¦68635 at Levo¦68636-Hamat¦68637 \add in the north\add*.
\v 22 \add They started\add* in the Negev¦68640, and¦68639 went¦68639 as far as Hevron where some of Anak's¦68650 descendents lived: Ahiman¦68646, Sheshay¦68647, Talmai¦68648. Hevron had been built¦68654 seven¦68652 years¦68653 \add ≈before\add* Tsoan¦68656 in Egypt¦68657 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add*.
\v 23 When¦68659 they got to¦68660 the¦68662 Eshkol¦68663 riverbed¦68662, they cut¦68664 off a branch¦68666 \add ≈with\add* a cluster¦68667 of grapes¦68668, and carried¦68670 it¦68670 on¦68671 a pole¦68671 between two¦68672 of them, \add ≈along with some\add* pomegranates¦68675 and figs¦68678.
\v 24 (That¦68681 place¦68680 was then called¦68682 Eshkol¦68684, \add meaning ‘cluster’\add*, because of the cluster \add of grapes\add* they'd taken from¦68691 there¦68691.)
\s2 The reports from the scouts
