\v 26 and went¦68703 to Kadesh¦68722 in the Paran¦68721 wilderness¦68720. There¦68717 they¦68703 reported back to Mosheh¦68706 and Aharon¦68709 and all¦68728 the assembled people¦68715, and showed¦68731 them¦68731 the fruit¦68734 from the land¦68735,
\v 27 and told \add #them\add*, “We¦68741 went¦68741 to the¦68744 land¦68744 where you¦68746 sent¦68746 us¦68746, and it is indeed flowing¦68748 with milk¦68749 and honey¦68750, and this¦68752 is its¦68754 fruit¦68754.
\v 28 However, the people living in that¦68761 land are powerful, and¦68763 the cities¦68763 are very¦68766 well fortified¦68764. Also¦68767, some of¦68769 the Anak¦68770 people group live there¦68772.
\v 29 The Amalekite people live in the Negev¦68777, and the Hittites¦68778, Yebusites¦68779, and Amorites¦68780 live in the hill country¦68782, and the Kanaanites¦68783 live along the coast and \add ≈along\add* the Yarden¦68790 \add !(Jordan¦68790) river\add*.”
\p
\v 30 Then¦68792 Kalev \add !(Caleb¦68793)\add* \add raised an arm\add* to quieten¦68792 the people¦68796 in front of Mosheh¦68799 \add ≈and stated\add*, “We'll certainly¦68801 go in there and take¦68803 it over, because¦68805 we're capable of \add going\add* against \add #them\add*.”
