\v 2 and then¦68890 they¦68900 \add started\add* to¦68901 protest against¦68894 Mosheh¦68893 and Aharon¦68896. They¦68899 \add ≈were all¦68902 saying¦68900\add*, “If¦68905 only we'd died¦68907 in Egypt¦68909 or¦68910 \add back there\add* in this¦68912 wilderness¦68911.
\v 3 Why¦68917 did Yahweh¦68918 bring¦68919 us to this¦68924 \add ≈place only to be slaughtered in¦68926 battle with¦68926 our wives¦68927 and¦68917 children being taken as\add* plunder¦68930? Wouldn't it be better for¦68933 us to return¦68934 to Egypt¦68935?”
\v 4 \add ≈So¦68937 they¦68937 said¦68937 to each other\add*, “Let's \add ≈choose a new leader¦68943\add* to take us back to Egypt¦68945.”
\p
\v 5 Then¦68947 Mosheh¦68948 and¦68947 Aharon¦68949 fell¦68947 \add ≈to their knees with their faces¦68952 bowed in¦68953 front¦68953 of¦68953 all¦68954 the assembled¦68956 Israelis¦68958\add*.
