\v 13 \add ≈But¦69100\add* Mosheh¦69101 \add ≈disagreed with¦69110\add* Yahweh¦69104, “Then¦69100 Egypt¦69106 will hear¦69105 about¦69110 how you¦69109 \add ≈used\add* your¦69110 power¦69110 to bring¦69109 \add #these\add* people¦69113 out from¦69115 among¦69115 them,
\v 14 and they'll¦69117 \add ≈report\add* to¦69118 the inhabitants of \add @Kanaan\add*, because¦69124 those \add ≡inhabitants\add* have¦69123 heard¦69123 that \add you\add*, Yahweh¦69127, are¦69128 \add right here\add* in¦69128 the middle of \add ≈us Israeli people¦69129\add*, and how your¦69139 cloud rests on¦69128 us, and how you lead \add ≈us\add* with¦69128 that pillar of cloud that becomes a pillar of fire¦69149 at¦69128 night¦69150.
\v 15 If you¦69152 \add ≈exterminate all the Israelis¦69155\add*, those nations¦69160 who've heard¦69163 about¦69166 your¦69166 fame will¦69159 say,
\v 16 ‘\add That\add* Yahweh¦69171 couldn't take those people¦69175 into¦69177 the land¦69179 that¦69180 he promised them, so he slaughtered¦69184 them in¦69185 the wilderness¦69185.’
