\v 23 \add ≈so there's no way\add* that they'll¦69285 \add ≈enter\add* the¦69288 land¦69288 that I¦69290 promised to their¦69291 ancestors¦69291. All¦69292 those¦69294 who¦69294 despised¦69294 me¦69294 won't¦69295 \add get to\add* \add ≈enter\add* it¦69296.
\v 24 \add ≈However,\add* my¦69298 servant¦69298 Kalev¦69299 \add !(Caleb¦69299)\add* has¦69301 a different spirit¦69302 with¦69304 him, and he wholeheartedly¦69305 followed¦69306 me¦69306, \add ≈so\add* I'll¦69307 take¦69316 him into¦69308 the¦69310 land¦69310 \add ≈that he explored\add*, and his¦69315 descendants¦69315 will¦69316 inherit¦69316 it.\x + \xo 14:24: \xt Josh 14:9-12.\x*
\v 25 The¦69318 Amalekites and Kanaanites¦69319 live in¦69321 the valleys¦69321. Tomorrow¦69322, you all must turn¦69323 and set¦69324 off towards the wilderness¦69326 via the \add ≈route to\add* the Red Sea¦69328.
