\v 14 If a \add ≈foreigner is staying with you all\add* or¦69864 living among¦69867 you for \add multiple\add* generations¦69868, and¦69869 they make an¦69871 offering¦69869 to¦69874 Yahweh¦69874 with a pleasing¦69873 aroma¦69871, then¦69859 they must¦69861 \add ≈follow the same instructions\add* as¦69875 all of you.
\v 15 \add Yes,\add* \add ≈the same regulations apply to both you and¦69884 the foreigners living among you all\add*. \add ≈That will always¦69887 apply—foreigners in front¦69892 of Yahweh¦69893 must¦69891 do the same\add* as all of you.
\v 16 One¦69896 \add set of\add* instructions and regulations for¦69900 \add both\add* you and the foreigner that lives among you all.
\p
\v 17 Then Yahweh¦69907 told Mosheh¦69910,
\v 18 “Tell¦69917 the \add ≈Israelis¦69916 that\add* when you get to the land¦69923 that I'm¦69925 taking you to,
