\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now\add* Korah¦70314 (son of Yitshar¦70317, son of Kehat, son of Levi¦70323) \add along with\add* Datan¦70324 and Aviram¦70325 (sons¦70326 of Eliav¦70327) and On¦70328 (son of Pelet¦70331)\x + \xo 16:1-35: \xt Jude 11.\x*
\v 2 \add ≈rebelled\add* against Mosheh¦70337 along with 250 \add ≈respected, Israeli¦70341\add* community leaders¦70344.
\v 3 They¦70352 \add ≈got together and challenged\add* Mosheh¦70355 and Aharon¦70358, “\add ≈You think you're great but¦70352 the¦70367 entire¦70365 community is¦70370 sacred¦70369 and has Yahweh among¦70370 us, so why¦70372 do¦70373 you consider yourselves¦70373 more important than Yahweh's¦70371 community?\add*”
\p
\v 4 \add ≈When¦70379\add* Mosheh¦70380 heard \add <that\add*, he¦70381 fell¦70381 \add ≈to his knees with his face¦70384 to the ground\add*
\v 5 and \add ≈responded\add* to Korah¦70389 and his \add ≈supporters\add*, “\add Tomorrow\add* morning¦70396 Yahweh will show who's sacred¦70406 and who belongs to him. \add ?≈Yahweh will present his chosen leader\add*. make¦70397 known¦70397 who is to him and the¦70406 holy¦70406 one, and he will present to him, and whom¦70410 he chooses¦70411 he will present to him.
\v 6 \add ≈So\add* Korah¦70423 and¦70424 \add ≈supporters\add*, bring incense burners
\v 7 and put¦70428 \add ≈burning¦70431 coals\add* and incense¦70434 in¦70429 them, and bring them to¦70435 \add ≈Yahweh's¦70436 presence\add* tomorrow¦70437. Then¦70428 the man¦70439 that Yahweh chooses¦70442 will be¦70445 the sacred¦70445 one. \add ≈It's you Levites who think you're\add* great.”
\p
\v 8 Then¦70452 Mosheh¦70453 told Korah¦70456, “\add ≈You Levites\add*, please¦70459 listen¦70457.
\v 9 Isn't¦70472 it¦70463 enough¦70463 for¦70464 you all that Yisrael's¦70469 god¦70468 separated you from the \add rest of\add* the Israeli¦70468 community to present you to him¦70475 to serve¦70485 in Yahweh's¦70481 residence and¦70482 to stand¦70482 in front¦70483 of the gatherings to minister to them¦70485?
\v 10 \add @Yahweh\add* has¦70487 presented you and¦70487 your¦70493 brothers¦70493, the \add other\add* \add ≈Levites\add* to approach \add <him\add*. Are you all wanting the priesthood¦70501 \add now\add* also¦70499?
\v 11 \add ≈So¦70503\add* it's Yahweh¦70511 that you and¦70505 your¦70507 group are opposing, not \add really\add* Aharon¦70512 that you're all¦70505 grumbling¦70517 about¦70507.”
\p
\v 12 Then¦70521 Mosheh¦70522 \add ≈summoned\add* Eliav's¦70527 sons¦70526 Datan¦70524 and¦70521 Aviram¦70525 \add ≈but¦70521 they¦70528 refused\add*, “We¦70530 won't¦70529 come¦70530.
\v 13 \add ≈Isn't it¦70532 enough¦70532\add* that you¦70534 brought¦70534 us \em out\em* of¦70536 a land¦70535 flowing¦70536 with¦70540 milk¦70537 and¦70538 honey¦70538, to¦70539 kill¦70539 us \add here\add* in¦70540 the wilderness¦70540, without also making yourself¦70543 the ruler¦70543 over¦70544 us?
\v 14 \add ≈What's more\add*, you didn't¦70550 bring¦70557 us into a land flowing¦70554 with milk¦70555 and honey¦70556 or give¦70558 us an¦70561 inheritance¦70561 of land and vineyards¦70563. Will¦70567 you gouge¦70567 out¦70567 the¦70564 eyes¦70564 of those¦70566 \add @Kanaanites\add* \add so that we can defeat them\add*? \add No,\add* we won't¦70550 come¦70569.”
\p
\v 15 \add That made\add* Mosheh¦70572 very angry and¦70571 he¦70574 told Yahweh¦70577, “Don't¦70578 \add ≈accept\add* their¦70583 grain offering¦70583. I've¦70588 \add never\add* taken¦70588 \add even\add* one¦70586 donkey¦70585 from¦70587 them \add ≈or done¦70590 anything bad to¦70590 any of¦70594\add* them.”
\p
\v 16 Then¦70596 Mosheh¦70597 told Korah¦70600, “You¦70601 and¦70596 all¦70602 your¦70604 group, \add ≈must appear in¦70606 front¦70606\add* of¦70606 Yahweh¦70607 tomorrow¦70611, \add ≈as will\add* Aharon¦70610.
