\v 21 “Get away from¦70684 \add ≈all those people\add*, then I¦70687 can destroy them¦70689 in an instant.”
\p
\v 22 \add ≈However,\add* \add @Mosheh and Aharon\add* fell¦70692 \add ≈to their knees with their faces¦70695 to the ground and interceded\add*, “God¦70697, \add you are\add* the god \add ≈who gives life to everything\add*. Will you be angry¦70710 at the entire¦70707 community \add because of\add* the sin¦70705 of one man¦70703?”
\v 23 \add ≈So\add* Yahweh¦70714 told Mosheh¦70717,
\v 24 “Tell the \add ≈people to¦70724 keep back from¦70726 the homes\add* of¦70727 Korah¦70729, Datan¦70730, and¦70731 Aviram¦70731.”
\p
\v 25 Then¦70733 Mosheh¦70734 \add ≈walked to¦70736\add* \add the homes of\add* Datan¦70738 and Aviram¦70739, and the \add ≈Israeli¦70742\add* elders¦70742 followed¦70740 behind him¦70741,
\v 26 and he¦70745 told the \add ≈people\add*, “Please¦70751 \add ≈keep back\add* from¦70752 the tents¦70753 of these¦70756 wicked¦70755 men¦70754, and don't¦70757 touch¦70759 anything of theirs, in case you get caught up in their¦70769 \add ≈disobedience\add*.”
\v 27 \add ≈So¦70771\add* \add @the rest of the Israelis\add* \add ≈kept back\add* from the residences of Korah¦70775, Datan, and Aviram. \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* Datan and Aviram had come¦70782 out of their tents¦70785, and were standing¦70783 at the entrances¦70784 with their wives¦70786 and children¦70787.
\p
\v 28 Then¦70790 Mosheh¦70791 said¦70790, “This¦70792 is how \add you'll all\add* known¦70793 that \add it was\add* Yahweh¦70796 \add ≈who selected me¦70797 for¦70798 this¦70792 role\add*—it's \add never\add* \add ≈been something that I aspired to\add*:
\v 29 If all these¦70816 men \add ≈die¦70815 a natural death¦70811 like¦70811 most people\add*, then Yahweh¦70824 didn't¦70823 \add ≈choose\add* me¦70825,
\v 30 \add ≈but¦70827\add* if Yahweh \add ≈does something new\add* and the¦70833 ground opens¦70832 its¦70836 mouth¦70836 and swallows¦70837 them¦70838 and their homes and tents and \add ≈all their possessions\add*, and if they¦70850 then go¦70845 down alive¦70846 into \add ≈their grave\add*, then you'll all know¦70848 that¦70849 it was because¦70849 these¦70852 men¦70851 rejected Yahweh.”
\p
\v 31 \add ≈As soon as Mosheh had finished¦70858 speaking¦70859\add*, the ground below \add @those¦70864 men\add* split¦70865 open¦70865
\v 32 and the¦70871 earth¦70871 opened¦70870 its¦70874 mouth¦70874 and swallowed¦70875 them¦70876 and their homes and every¦70881 man who¦70884 \add ≈backed\add* Korah¦70885 along with all¦70887 \add &their\add* property¦70889.
\v 33 They¦70898 went¦70891 down¦70891 alive¦70897 to \add ≈their grave\add*, along with everything they owned, and then¦70891 the ground covered¦70899 over¦70900 them¦70900 and they \add ≈vanished\add* from¦70903 the \add ≈community\add*.
\v 34 All¦70908 the people who were around¦70910 them¦70910 fled¦70911 \add away\add* \add ≈screaming because¦70913 they¦70911 were afraid of¦70912 getting swallowed¦70917 by the earth¦70918 as well\add*.
\p
\v 35 Then¦70920 Yahweh¦70923 \add ≈sent\add* fire¦70920 that consumed the¦70926 250 men who¦70929 were¦70929 presenting incense¦70930.
\s1 The incense burners
\rem /s1 The Fire Pans
\p
\v 36 Then Yahweh told Mosheh,
\v 37 “Tell the priest Eleazar (Aharon's son) to \add ≈collect the incense pans\add* from \add ≈those who were burnt\add*, and scatter the \add ≈coals far away\add* because they're sacred.
\v 38 The pans of those who \add ≈rebelled at the expense of their own lives\add* must be hammered into thin plates \add ≈to be attached\add* to the altar, because they presented them \add ≈in front\add* of Yahweh and \add now\add* they're sacred, and they'll become a \add ≈reminder\add* for the \add ≈Israelis\add*.
\v 39 \add ≈So\add* the priest Eleazar took the bronze incense burners that had been presented by those men who'd been burnt up, and they were hammered into a plating for the altar
\v 40 for a memorial for the \add ≈Israelis\add* just as Yahweh had told him via Mosheh. That's a reminder that no one who's not a descendant of Aharon is allowed to approach Yahweh with incense burners, so they don't end up like Korah and his \add ≈supporters\add*.
\s1 The people complain and cause a plague
\rem /s1 Aaron Saves the People
\p
\v 41 \add ≈However,\add* the next day the \add ≈Israelis\add* complained about Mosheh and Aharon, “\add ≈It was you who\add* killed Yahweh's people.”
\v 42 \add ≈But\add* as the community gathered \add there\add* against Mosheh and Aharon, they \add ≈looked across\add* to the \add ≈sacred\add* tent, and wow, the cloud covered over it and Yahweh's \add ≈brilliance\add* appeared.
\v 43 Mosheh and Aharon went \add over\add* to the front of the \add ≈sacred\add* tent,
\v 44 and Yahweh told Mosheh,
\v 45 “Get away from this \add ≈gathering\add* and then I'll finish them \add ≈in an instant\add*.”
\p \add ≈But\add* \add @Mosheh and Aharon\add* fell \add ≈to their knees with their faces to the ground\add*,
\v 46 and Mosheh told Aharon, “Take the incense burner, and put fire in it from the altar and incense, and take it quickly to the \add ≈people\add* and make atonement for them, because Yahweh's rage is \add already\add* \add ≈burning\add*—the \add ≈deadly disease\add* has begun.”
\v 47 \add ≈So\add* Aharon took it as Mosheh had told \add <him\add* and ran into the middle of the \add ≈people\add*. Wow, the \add ≈deadly disease\add* had already begun, \add ≈so he burnt\add* incense and made atonement for \add *them\add*.
\v 48 He stood between those who were dying and those still alive, and the \add ≈deadly disease\add* was restrained.
\v 49 There were 14,700 \add >people\add* who died from the \add ≈deadly disease\add*, in addition to those who'd died due to Korah's \add ≈rebellion\add*.
\v 50 Then Aharon returned to Mosheh at the \add ≈sacred\add* tent entrance, \add ≈as\add* the \add ≈disease\add* had been \add ≈stopped\add*.
\c 17
\s1 The budding of Aharon's rod
\rem /s1 Aaron's Walking Stick; The Budding of Aaron's Staff; The Budding of Aaron's Rod
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦70935 told Mosheh¦70938,
\v 2 “Tell the \add ≈Israelis\add* to bring you twelve staffs—one from¦70954 each ancestral \add tribe\add* with the leader's name inscribed on it,
\v 3 and inscribe Aharon's name on¦70970 the staff for the \add ≈Levites\add* so there's one for each tribe.
\v 4 Put them \add all\add* in the \add ≈sacred\add* tent in front of¦70994 the \add ≈sacred box\add* where I meet with you,
\v 5 and then the staff of¦71005 the man¦71012 that I choose \add to be the priest\add* will¦71025 sprout. Then the \add ≈people¦71005\add* can stop complaining to me about¦71005 you.”
\p
\v 6 \add ≈So Mosheh¦71047 passed the message on to¦71051 the Israeli¦71041\add* leaders and they¦71037 gave him one staff for each leader—\add ≈a total¦71038 of¦71056 twelve including¦71037 Aharon's¦71050 one\add*,
\v 7 and Mosheh¦71065 \add ≈laid\add* them \add ≈in front\add* of¦71072 Yahweh¦71079 in the \add ≈sacred¦71072\add* tent¦71072.
\p
\v 8 Then the next day when Mosheh¦71083 went¦71082 to the \add ≈sacred¦71088\add* tent¦71088, wow, he saw that Aharon's¦71084 staff (\add ≈representing\add* Levi tribe) had sprouted, plus¦71082 it had blossomed and produced a flower and ripened almonds!\x + \xo 17:8-10: \xt Heb 9:4.\x*
\v 9 Mosheh¦71097 took all the staffs \add ≈out of the tent\add* to the people \add ≈to look at\add* and¦71093 \add ≈each of the leaders\add* took back his own staff,
\v 10 then Yahweh told Mosheh, “Put Aharon's staff \add back\add* \add ≈in front of¦71102 the sacred chest\add*. \add ≈Keep it there as a reminder to\add* \add any\add* \add ≈rebels to stop complaining against me so¦71105 they¦71108 won't\add* die.”
\v 11 \add ≈So¦71118\add* Moses¦71115 did what Yahweh¦71143 had commanded.
\p
\v 12 Then the \add ≈Israelis¦71163\add* \add ≈complained\add* to Mosheh¦71153, “Wow¦71153, \add ≈we're done for—it's clear that we're all going to die\add*!
\v 13 Everyone who goes close to Yahweh's residence \add ≈gets killed\add*. \add ≈Won't we all die\add*?”
\c 18
\s1 The work of priests and Levites
\rem /s1 Duties of Priests and Levites; Responsibility of Priests and Levites
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦71452 told Aharon¦71455 \add !(Aaron¦71455)\add*, “You¦71456 and your \add ≈Levite brothers and cousins\add* and \add all\add* your descendants must bear the \add ≈imperfections\add* of the \add ≈sacred¦71466 tent¦71466\add*, and you and your sons¦71468 must bear the \add ≈imperfections\add* of your priesthood¦71474.
\v 2 Bring your \add ≈Levite¦71481\add* brothers¦71479 (your father's tribe) to \add ≈work closely with¦71485\add* you and to assist¦71488 you \add as\add* you and your sons¦71490 \add ≈perform your duties at\add* the \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦71493.
\v 3 They¦71496 must¦71496 look after the tent¦71501, however, they mustn't approach the \add ≈furnishings or utensils\add*, or the altar¦71509, so that both¦71515 you¦71497 and¦71496 they won't¦71510 die¦71514.
\v 4 Then¦71522 must¦71522 \add ≈work¦71531 closely with\add* you¦71523 and¦71522 \add ≈take care\add* of \add ≈all the duties to do with\add* the \add ≈sacred¦71528\add* tent¦71532, \add ≈but¦71522\add* no \add ≈outsider¦71533\add* \add ≈is allowed to approach\add*.
\v 5 You¦71554 \add priests\add* will¦71539 \add ≈take care\add* of¦71541 the sacred¦71542 place¦71542 and the altar¦71545, and then¦71539 there won't¦71546 be¦71548 anymore fury against¦71549 the \add ≈Israeli¦71553 people¦71553\add*.
\v 6 \add ≈Now listen\add*, I've¦71558 taken¦71558 your brothers¦71561 the Levites¦71562 \add ≈out from¦71563 the rest of the Israelis¦71564\add* as a gift¦71567 for you—they're¦71568 given to \add ≈do the duties\add* at the \add ≈sacred¦71574\add* tent¦71574.
\v 7 \add ≈However,\add* it's you¦71579 and your¦71578 sons¦71578 who \add ≈are the priests\add* who must serve¦71590 for things to do with the altar¦71587 and inside¦71588 the curtain¦71589. Your priesthood¦71596 is a gift¦71592 of¦71596 service¦71591, and any \add ≈outsider¦71597\add* who approaches¦71598 must be¦71599 executed¦71599.”
\rem /s1 Offerings for Priests and Levites; Support for the Priests and Levites; The Priests' Portion; The Share of the Priests
\p
\v 8 Then Yahweh¦71603 told Aharon¦71606, “\add ≈Also listen\add*, I've put you in charge¦71613 of \add ≈looking after\add* the sacred¦71617 offerings¦71614 \add ≈to me\add*. I've given¦71623 them¦71623 to you and¦71625 your sons¦71625 as your \add ≈permanent¦71628 income\add*.
\v 9 Every offering¦71641 apart from the burnt offerings, will belong¦71632 to¦71642 you. That includes their grain¦71644 offerings, their sin¦71647 offerings, and their guilt¦71650 offerings. \add ≈Once they're given, they become sacred¦71635,\add* and they're for you and your¦71658 sons¦71658.
\v 10 You and \add ≈the males in your families\add* may eat that sacred offering \add ≈but do remember that it's sacred\add*.
\p
\v 11 “\add ≈In¦71682 addition¦71673,\add* the \add people's\add* raised offerings belong¦71675 to you, and¦71673 they are \add ≈permanently given¦71684 to your entire families\add* to eat—everyone¦71691 who's ‘clean¦71693’ may eat them.
\p
\v 12 “All the best¦71699 of¦71699 the fresh¦71700 oil¦71700, and the new¦71704 wine¦71704 and grain¦71705 that¦71707 they¦71709 give to Yahweh¦71710, I¦71712 give to you.
\v 13 The¦71714 first¦71714 \add ≈portions of¦71714 all¦71715 their¦71718 harvests\add* that¦71719 they¦71721 bring¦71721 to Yahweh¦71722, belong¦71724 to you—everyone¦71725 in¦71718 your¦71728 \add ≈families\add* who's ‘clean¦71727’ may eat¦71729 them.
\p
\v 14 “Everything¦71731 throughout Yisrael¦71734 that's dedicated \add to Yahweh\add* will¦71736 belong¦71736 to you.\x + \xo 18:14: \xt Lev 27:28.\x*
\p
\v 15 “Every¦71738 firstborn¦71740 \add male\add* \add ≈baby\add*, as well as animals, will belong¦71751 to Yahweh¦71748, \add however\add* you must¦71747 buy back the \add ≈human¦71749 babies\add* as well as the firstborns¦71762 from the ‘unclean¦71765’ livestock¦71764.
\v 16 \add ≈The babies\add* must¦71772 be¦71774 bought back when they're one month¦71771 old, paying five¦71775 silver¦71774 coins \add ≈of the proper weight according to the scales at¦71773 the sacred¦71778 tent¦71778\add*.
\v 17 \add ≈However,\add* the firstborn¦71784 cows or sheep or goats can't¦71795 be bought back. They are sacred¦71797—you must¦71796 sprinkle¦71802 their blood¦71801 on¦71803 the altar¦71805 and¦71806 burn their fat¦71808 as an¦71811 offering¦71810 that's a soothing¦71812 aroma¦71811 for¦71813 Yahweh¦71813.
\v 18 Their¦71815 meat¦71815 will¦71816 belong¦71816 to¦71818 you¦71818, just like¦71819 the breast¦71819 or the right¦71822 thigh¦71821 of¦71821 the wave offerings¦71820 are yours¦71823.
\v 19 All sacred¦71829 donations by the \add ≈Israelis¦71832\add*, I've \add ≈permanently\add* given¦71836 to you and your \add ≈children\add* to eat—it's an \add ≈irrevocable agreement¦71844 with¦71840\add* Yahweh¦71835 for you and your \add future\add* ancestors.”
\s1 The Levites' share
\p
\v 20 Yahweh¦71855 \add also\add* told Aharon¦71858, “You¦71861 \add priests\add* won't¦71860 inherit¦71861 \add ≈any land¦71859 or property\add*—I¦71868 am¦71869 your share and¦71854 your inheritance¦71870 \add ≈among¦71867 the Israelis¦71872\add*.
\rem /s1 The Share of the Levites
\p
\v 21 For¦71884 an¦71884 inheritance¦71884 for the \add ≈Levites\add*, I've given them all the tenths \add ≈given by the Israelis¦71883\add* as their inheritance in¦71883 exchange for their service¦71890 at¦71883 the \add ≈sacred¦71894\add* tent¦71894.
\v 22 The¦71902 \add ≈other Israelis¦71901\add* mustn't approach that tent¦71905 \add or\add* they'll¦71899 \add ≈incur guilt\add* and¦71897 die¦71909,
\v 23 \add ≈but¦71911\add* the Levites¦71912 must serve¦71911 at¦71925 the \add ≈sacred¦71917\add* tent¦71917 and¦71911 they must bear¦71920 their¦71921 \add ≈inadequacies\add*. That¦71927 order \add ≈applies for all future generations¦71924\add*, \add ≈including¦71919\add* the not¦71928 inheriting¦71929 any land \add ≈like the other Israelis¦71926\add*.
\v 24 \add That's\add* because¦71932 I've¦71949 given¦71943 the Levites¦71944 that tenth that the \add ≈other Israelis¦71936\add* offer¦71940 to Yahweh¦71941 as a donation. That's why I said¦71949 that they¦71955 won't¦71954 receive \add ≈any other inheritance¦71955\add*.”
\s1 The Levites' contribution
\rem /s1 The Levites' Tithe
\p
\v 25 Then Yahweh¦71960 told Mosheh¦71963,
\v 26 “Tell the Levites¦71968: ‘When¦71966 you all receive the tenth from the \add ≈Israelis¦71976\add* that I've given¦71983 to you as you inheritance¦71986, then¦71966 you must¦71969 offer¦71987 a tenth of that tenth as a donation to Yahweh¦71990.
\v 27 That will¦71996 be¦71996 considered as your contribution¦71998 \add just\add* as if it¦71996 was grain¦71999 from the threshing¦72002 floor¦72002, or \add ≈juice\add* from the wine-pressing¦72006 \add pit\add*.
\v 28 \add ≈So\add* when you all offer¦72009 that donation from all the tenths that you receive from the \add ≈Israelis¦72020\add*, it must¦72009 then be given¦72022 as Yahweh's¦72014 contribution¦72026 to¦72028 the priest¦72029 Aharon¦72028. DOUBLE-CHECK
\v 29 When an offering¦72033 is presented to Yahweh¦72038, it¦72045 must¦72033 be \add ≈the¦72037 best¦72041 parts of whatever is given\add*.’
\v 30 Also¦72055 tell them¦72048, ‘When¦72047 you¦72049 all present \add ≈the best¦72052 of¦72052 what was given\add*, it'll¦72054 be as \add ≈it's come straight\add* from the threshing¦72057 floor¦72057 or the wine-pressing¦72059 \add pit\add*.
\v 31 \add The rest\add* is¦72070 for your wages for the service¦72074 you all do at¦72075 the \add ≈sacred¦72075\add* tent¦72075, and¦72061 you all can eat¦72061 it \add ≈wherever you want to\add*.
\v 32 \add ≈After¦72093 donating the best¦72086 tenth from it\add*, you won't¦72078 incur guilt for what you all do with¦72083 the rest of it, \add ≈however\add* you all mustn't defile any sacred¦72090 things or you'll die¦72097.’ ”
\c 19
\s1 The red cow's ashes
\rem /s1 The Water of Purification; Ashes of the Red Cow; Ceremony of the Red Heifer; The Water of Cleansing
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦72101 told Mosheh¦72104 and¦72105 Aharon¦72107,
\v 2 “This is¦72111 \add ≈a new\add* law¦72112 that Yahweh¦72116 has commanded¦72115, ‘Tell the¦72122 \add ≈Israelis¦72122\add* that¦72113 they¦72124 must bring¦72124 you¦72125 an unblemished¦72128 red¦72127 heifer¦72126 \add ≈with¦72132 no¦72128 defects¦72128\add* \add ≈and¦72124 that has never had a yoke¦72139 on¦72132 its neck\add*.
\v 3 Give¦72141 it to¦72143 the priest¦72146 Eleazar¦72145, and he¦72147 must¦72141 take¦72147 it outside¦72151 the camp¦72152 and have \add someone\add* slaughter¦72153 it \add ≈in front¦72155 of him¦72155\add*.
\v 4 Then¦72157 Eleazar¦72158 must¦72157 get some¦72160 of its¦72170 blood¦72160 with¦72161 his¦72161 finger¦72161 seven¦72171 times¦72172 and¦72157 \add ≈flick\add* it onto the ground \add ≈directly in¦72161 front¦72165\add* of the \add ≈sacred¦72167\add* tent¦72167.
\v 5 Then¦72174 \add ≈while he¦72174 watches\add*, they must¦72174 \add completely\add* burn¦72191 the¦72177 heifer¦72177—its skin¦72181 and flesh¦72184, and \add including\add* its blood¦72187 and dung¦72190.
\v 6 \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* the priest¦72194 must¦72193 take¦72193 some cedar¦72196 wood¦72195, hyssop¦72197, and scarlet¦72199 wool, and throw¦72200 them¦72200 into¦72201 \add the fire\add* where the cow is burning¦72204.
\v 7 Then¦72207 the priest¦72209 must¦72207 wash¦72210 his¦72211 clothes¦72208 and¦72207 bathe¦72210. After¦72213 that, he can return to the camp¦72217, \add ≈but¦72207\add* \add *he'll¦72207\add* be¦72218 ‘unclean¦72218’ until¦72220 that evening¦72222.
\v 8 The¦72224 \add man\add* who¦72224 burnt¦72224 \add @the¦72224 cow\add* must¦72226 \add also\add* wash¦72226 his¦72227 clothes¦72227 and bathe¦72229, and he¦72232 will¦72232 \add also\add* be¦72232 ‘unclean¦72232’ until¦72233 that evening¦72235.
\v 9 A¦72253 ‘clean¦72240’ man¦72239 must¦72237 collect the cow's ashes and¦72237 place them¦72244 in¦72247 a \add ≈sacred\add* place outside¦72245 the camp¦72246 where they can be used for water¦72255 for purification for the \add ≈Israelis¦72251\add* to¦72255 purify from \add ≈disobedience\add*.
\v 10 Then¦72260 that man who¦72261 collected the ashes must¦72260 \add also\add* wash¦72260 his¦72268 clothes¦72268 and be¦72269 ‘unclean¦72269’ until¦72270 that evening¦72272. Those¦72275 regulations¦72279 will¦72273 permanently apply both to \add ≈Israelis¦72274\add* and to foreigners living among¦72278 them¦72278.
\s1 Contact with a corpse
\rem /s1 Contact with a Corpse
\p
\v 11 “ ‘\add #All those\add* who touch¦72282 a dead¦72283, human body¦72283 will¦72288 be¦72288 ‘unclean¦72288’ for seven¦72289 days¦72290.
\v 12 On the third¦72297 day, they must¦72293 purify themselves, and¦72298 then they'll be ‘clean’ on the seventh day. (If¦72301 they don't¦72303 purify themselves, they'll won't¦72303 become ‘clean’ on that seventh day—
\v 13 if they've touched¦72314 a dead¦72315, human¦72317 body¦72316 and don't¦72321 purify¦72322 themselves, that would defile Yahweh's¦72326 residence, and \add so\add* they must¦72320 be¦72328 \add ?≈permanently removed from the camp\add*. If¦72331 the purifying water¦72333 wasn't sprinkled¦72337 on them, that ‘uncleanness¦72342’ will remain on them.)
\p
\v 14 “ ‘This is¦72346 the regulation if¦72348 a person dies¦72350 in a tent: Everyone¦72354 who was in the tent, and¦72358 everyone¦72352 that enters \add afterwards\add*, will all be¦72362 ‘unclean¦72362’ for seven¦72363 days¦72364,
\v 15 and¦72366 every¦72366 container that¦72369 doesn't have its lid on¦72374 becomes ‘unclean¦72375’.
\v 16 \add ≈Out in\add* the countryside¦72385, who¦72379 touches¦72381 the corpse of¦72384 someone killed¦72386 in a fight, or any dead¦72390 human¦72394 body¦72390 or bone¦72393 or grave¦72396, will¦72397 be¦72397 ‘unclean¦72397’ for seven¦72398 days¦72399.
\v 17 \add ≈Someone\add* must¦72401 take¦72401 some of the ashes¦72403 from that burnt¦72404 cow, and¦72401 put them into a jar with some fresh, running water¦72408, then¦72401 \add pour some of it over them\add*.
\v 18 Then¦72414 a man who's ‘clean¦72419’ must¦72414 dip¦72416 some hyssop¦72415 in that water¦72417 and sprinkle¦72420 it onto the tent¦72423 and all¦72426 the containers \add in it\add* and everyone¦72431 who lives in it or who touched¦72438 the body¦72443 or the bone¦72439 or grave¦72445.
\v 19 On the third¦72453 day, that ‘clean¦72448’ man must sprinkle¦72447 \add ≡that water¦72462\add* on the ‘unclean’ ones, and then¦72447 must purify¦72456 them on the seventh¦72455 day. Then¦72447 he¦72459 \add himself\add* must wash¦72459 his¦72460 clothes¦72460 and bathe¦72461, and will¦72463 be¦72463 ‘unclean’ until that evening¦72464.
\p
\v 20 “ ‘Anyone¦72481 who's¦72467 ‘unclean’ and¦72466 doesn't purify¦72471 themself, that person¦72466 will be¦72472 \add ?≈permanently removed from¦72475 the camp\add* because¦72477 they've made¦72482 Yahweh's¦72481 sanctuary¦72480 ‘unclean’. They didn't¦72470 sprinkle¦72487 that purifying water¦72483 on¦72488 themself, so they \add remain\add* ‘unclean’.
\v 21 That will be a \add ≈permanent¦72496\add* regulation¦72495. The¦72497 person who's¦72497 had the purifying water sprinkled on¦72504 them must¦72492 wash¦72501 their clothes¦72502, and¦72492 any person who \add ≈sprinkles\add* the water will be ‘unclean¦72506’ until¦72507 that evening¦72509.
\v 22 Anything touched¦72514 by an ‘unclean’ person becomes ‘unclean’, and¦72519 anyone¦72519 who touches¦72520 an ‘unclean’ person will¦72521 become ‘unclean’ until¦72522 that evening¦72524.
\c 20
\s1 Water from the Kadesh rock
\rem /s1 The Waters of Meribah; Events at Kadesh; Moses Strikes the Rock; Water From the Rock
\r (Exo. 17:1-7)
\p
\v 1 Then in¦72537 the first¦72538 month¦72537 \add of the next year\add*, all the \add ≈Israelis¦72530\add* entered the Tsin¦72536 \add (‘Thorny’ or ‘Thirsty’)\add* wilderness¦72534 and the people¦72540 \add ≈camped\add* at¦72537 Kadesh¦72541. \add While they were\add* there, Miryam¦72544 died¦72542, and was¦72545 buried¦72545 there.
\p
\v 2 \add ≈However,\add* there was no water¦72551 \add ≈to¦72552 drink,\add* \add ≈so the people\add* came against¦72557 Mosheh¦72556 and¦72548 Aharon¦72559\x + \xo 20:2-13: \xt Exo 17:1-7.\x*
\v 3 and¦72561 complained, “\add ≈It¦72565 would have¦72569 been better if¦72568 we'd died¦72569 in¦72570 front¦72572 of Yahweh¦72573 along with¦72570 our¦72571 relatives\add* \add back there\add*.
\v 4 Why¦72575 did¦72576 you two bring¦72576 Yahweh's¦72580 people here to die¦72585 in this wilderness¦72583, along with our¦72588 livestock¦72588?
\v 5 Why¦72590 did¦72591 you bring us out of Egypt¦72592 to bring us to this¦72599 miserable place¦72602? There's no \add ≈grain\add* or figs¦72604, and¦72590 no grapes or pomegranates¦72606. There's \add not even\add* water¦72607 to drink¦72609!”
\v 6 Then¦72611 Mosheh¦72612 and Aharon¦72613 went¦72611 from¦72614 \add there\add* in¦72614 front¦72614 of¦72614 the people to the entrance¦72618 to the \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦72619, where they¦72621 fell¦72621 \add ≈to their knees with their faces¦72624 to the ground\add*, and Yahweh's¦72628 brilliance appeared¦72625 to them¦72629.
\p
\v 7 Then Yahweh¦72633 told Mosheh¦72636,
\v 8 “Take \add &Aharon's¦72648\add* staff¦72642, then the two of you¦72647 must¦72650 command \add that\add* rock¦72653 to \add ≈pour out\add* water. Then water will come out of it, and both the people and the animals will \add have plenty to\add* drink¦72664.”
\p
\v 9 \add ≈So¦72672\add* Mosheh¦72673 took¦72672 the¦72676 staff¦72676 from¦72677 \add ≈Yahweh's¦72678 residence\add* like he¦72672 was told¦72680 to¦72677.
\v 10 Then¦72682 \add *the two of them\add* gathered¦72682 the people in front¦72690 of the rock and¦72682 told them, “Listen¦72694 now \add ≈you bunch of rebels¦72697\add*—do we¦72702 have to bring¦72702 water¦72704 out of this rock for¦72703 you?”
