\p \add ≈Now\add* Tsipor's¦73699 son¦73697 Balak¦73696 was¦73700 Moav's¦73678 king¦73700 at that¦73703 time¦73702,
\v 5 and he¦73705 sent¦73705 messengers¦73706 to Beor's¦73712 son¦73710 Bileam¦73709 \add !(Balaam¦73709)\add* at Petor¦73713 (which¦73714 was their tribal land¦73718 near the \add Euphrates\add* river¦73717). He¦73736 \add ≈requested help\add*, saying¦73725, “Listen, \add ≈there's a population here\add* that¦73714 came¦73728 out¦73728 from¦73729 Egypt¦73729. Wow, they've covered¦73731 the \add ≈entire surface in this region¦73718\add* and they're living¦73737 \add ≈opposite\add* me.\x + \xo 22:5: \xt Num 31:8; 2Pe 2:15-16; Jude 11.\x*
\v 6 \add ≈So¦73740\add* now¦73740 please¦73743 \add ≈come¦73741 and\add* curse this people¦73749 group for me because they are more numerous than us, \add then\add* perhaps¦73756 I'll¦73757 be able¦73757 to¦73758 \add ≈attack\add* them and drive¦73761 them out¦73761 of the¦73764 \add ≈area\add*, because I know¦73766 that¦73772 anyone you bless¦73770 will be blessed¦73771, and those who you curse will be cursed¦73774.”
