\p
\v 1 Then¦77694 Mosheh¦77702 \add !(Moses¦77690)\add* \add ≈gave\add* the¦77693 \add ≈Israeli¦77693 leaders\add* \add ≈these further instructions¦77698 from\add* Yahweh¦77699,
\v 2 “If a man makes a solemn promise to Yahweh¦77719, or makes a binding vow on his own life, he mustn't dishonour \add ≈what he said¦77714\add*—he must follow whatever came out of his mouth.\x + \xo 30:2: \xt Deu 23:21-23; Mat 5:33.\x*
\p
\v 3 If¦77723 a \add ≈young\add* woman who is \add ≈still living with her parents\add* solemnly promises to Yahweh¦77727 \add <to do¦77744 something\add*,
\v 4 and \add ≡if¦77748\add* her father¦77756 hears her make the binding¦77753 vow on¦77757 her life and he remains silent, then her vow and \add ≈all her obligations¦77754\add* will stand.
\v 5 \add ≈However,\add* if her father forbids her \add ≈when\add* he¦77760 hears¦77760 her, then that¦77766 vow¦77764 and \add ≈its obligations¦77780\add* won't stand, and Yahweh will forgive her, because her father \add ≈stepped in\add*.
\p
\v 6 If¦77809 she¦77803 \add ≈gets engaged or married while a vow or thoughtless promise still holds\add*,
\v 7 and her \add !(future)\add* husband¦77824 hears about¦77825 it and remains silent that¦77830 day, then her vow and or¦77827 thoughtless promise will stand.
\v 8 \add ≈However,\add* if her \add !(future)\add* husband¦77838 forbids her \add ≈when\add* he hears¦77840 her, then that¦77846 vow and \add ≈its obligations¦77845\add* won't stand¦77843, and Yahweh will forgive her.
\p
\v 9 \add ≈If¦77875\add* a widow or a woman who has¦77871 been divorced \add ≈makes a promise, she must¦77859 do what she promised\add*.
\p
\v 10 \add ≈If a married woman\add* makes a solemn promise, or makes a binding¦77887 vow¦77881 on her¦77890 own life,
\v 11 and her husband¦77898 hears about¦77897 it \add ≈but¦77895\add* says nothing and doesn't forbid her, then her vow and \add ≈all her obligations¦77903\add* will stand.
\v 12 \add ≈However,\add* if he actually nullifies it when he hears¦77910 about¦77918 it, any promise that¦77924 she¦77926 pronounced or binding¦77926 vow on her life, won't¦77914 stand. Her¦77920 husband¦77911 has¦77926 nullified them and Yahweh will forgive her,
\v 13 \add so\add* every vow and its obligations¦77947 can either be nullified¦77952 or confirmed by her¦77946 husband.
\v 14 If her¦77970 husband¦77970 has stayed silent for \add ≈several days\add*, that will confirm¦77969 all her vows and/or obligations¦77965 because he \add ≈said nothing\add*.
\v 15 \add ≈However,\add* if¦77974 he \add ≈cancels\add* them \add sometime\add* after he'd heard¦78005 about¦77987 them, then he will bear her¦77989 guilt.
\p
\v 16 Those are the instructions that Yahweh \add ≈gave\add* Mosheh \add about promises\add* between a man and his wife, \add and\add* between a father and his \add ≈unmarried\add* daughter \add ≈living at home\add*.
\c 31
