\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦78042 told Mosheh¦78045 \add !(Moses¦78045)\add*,
\v 2 “Avenge¦78048 the Midyanites for what they did to \add you\add* \add ≈Israelis¦78050\add*. After that, you'll¦78055 \add ≈go to join your¦78058 ancestors\add*.”
\p
\v 3 \add ≈So¦78060\add* Mosheh¦78061 told the¦78064 people¦78064, “Equip¦78078 some of your men¦78068 to battle¦78069 against Midyan¦78073 to \add ≈execute¦78074\add* Yahweh's¦78077 vengeance¦78075 on¦78078 \add *them\add*—
\v 4 one thousand men from each tribe¦78085 to go to war¦78088.”
\p
\v 5 \add ≈So¦78092\add* a thousand men were¦78090 conscripted¦78090 from¦78091 each tribe¦78094—twelve thousand equipped¦78099 for battle¦78100
\v 6 and¦78102 Mosheh¦78104 sent¦78102 them off to war¦78107. The priest¦78115 Pinehas (Eleazar's¦78114 son¦78112) went with them, taking some sacred¦78118 objects as well as the signal trumpets¦78119.
\v 7 Then¦78123 they fought¦78123 Midyan¦78126 just¦78127 as¦78127 Yahweh¦78129 had¦78128 commanded¦78128 Mosheh¦78132, and¦78133 they killed¦78133 every¦78134 male¦78136.
\v 8 \add Among them,\add* they killed¦78142 five¦78161 Midyan¦78141 kings¦78162: Evi¦78148, Rekem¦78151, Tsur¦78154, Hur¦78157, and¦78138 Reva, in¦78170 addition¦78138 to Beor's¦78168 son¦78166 Bileam¦78165 \add !(Balaam¦78165)\add*.
\p
\v 9 The¦78173 \add ≈Israelis¦78175\add* took the¦78178 Midyan¦78179 women¦78178 and children captive¦78172, and took all their cattle¦78186, \add ≈sheep and goats\add*, and all their \add ≈possessions as plunder¦78197\add*,
\v 10 then¦78199 they¦78208 burnt¦78208 down all¦78200 their cities¦78202 and houses and camps¦78207.
\v 11 They¦78211 took¦78211 all¦78214 the spoil¦78216 and plunder¦78220 including¦78217 the people¦78221 and animals back,
\v 12 and brought¦78224 it to Mosheh¦78227 and the priest¦78231 Eleazar¦78230, and to the \add ≈assembled Israelis¦78235\add* who were \add all still\add* camped on the Moav¦78253 plains¦78252 beside the Yarden¦78257 river opposite Yeriho¦78258 \add !(Jericho¦78258)\add*.
\s1 Purifying the returning warriors
