\p
\v 13 Mosheh¦78262 and the priest¦78264 Eleazar¦78263 and all¦78265 the \add ≈Israeli\add* leaders¦78267 left the camp¦78273 to¦78269 meet¦78269 them¦78269,
\v 14 \add ≈but¦78275\add* Mosheh¦78276 was¦78275 angry¦78275 at the top army¦78279 leaders who¦78284 were coming back from¦78285 the battle¦78286.
\v 15 “Why¦78290 did you allow all the women to live¦78291?” \add *he\add* asked them¦78289.
\v 16 “They're the \add ≈very ones who did what\add* Bileam¦78302 \add !(Balaam¦78302)\add* \add ≈suggested to urge the people to be unfaithful¦78305\add* to Yahweh at¦78301 Peor¦78311, \add ≈leading to\add* the \add ≈deadly disease\add* \add that struck\add* Yahweh's¦78306 \add ≈people\add*.\x + \xo 31:16: \xt Num 25:1-9.\x*
