\v 18 \add ≈spare only the¦78333 young¦78333, unmarried girls\add* for¦78342 yourselves¦78342.
\p
\v 19 “Then¦78344 everyone¦78351 who's killed¦78351 someone¦78352 or touched¦78355 a dead body must stay outside¦78346 the camp¦78347 for seven¦78348 days¦78349. On the third¦78359 day, you¦78357 all must purify¦78357 yourselves¦78357, and¦78344 \add again\add* on¦78356 the seventh day \add but this time\add* including¦78353 your captives¦78363.
\v 20 \add Also,\add* you¦78382 all must¦78382 purify¦78382 all your clothes, plus¦78368 anything \add else\add* made of leather or goats' hair¦78376 or wood¦78381.”
\p
\v 21 Then the priest¦78387 Eleazar¦78386 told¦78399 the \add ≈warriors¦78390\add* who'd gone¦78392 to¦78393 battle¦78393, “This¦78394 is¦78395 what Yahweh¦78400 has instructed¦78399 Mosheh¦78403:
\v 22 Only the gold¦78408, silver¦78411, bronze¦78414, iron¦78417, tin¦78420, and¦78421 lead¦78423,
\v 23 must pass through fire to make it ‘clean¦78434’. Nevertheless¦78435, it must still be¦78434 purified¦78438 with the \add special\add* purifying¦78438 water¦78436, along with anything that¦78428 wouldn't \add ≈handle\add* the fire.
\v 24 On the seventh¦78451 day¦78450, you all must¦78448 wash¦78448 your clothes¦78449 and then¦78448 you'll be ‘clean¦78452’ and \add ≈be allowed to¦78455 reenter\add* the camp¦78457.
\s1 Dividing the plunder
