\v 5 If¦78966 we've¦78968 \add ≈earnt\add* your favour¦78969, let¦78971 this land¦78974 be given¦78971 to your servants¦78976 for \add ≈us to own¦78977\add*, \add rather than forcing us\add* to cross¦78980 over¦78980 the Yarden¦78983 \add river with all the other tribes\add*.”
\p
\v 6 “It¦78985 wouldn't be right for your \add ≈fellow Israelis\add* to go¦78993 to war \add ≈while\add* you all \add just\add* stay here¦78997,” Mosheh¦78986 told them.
\v 7 “\add ≈So¦78999\add* why do¦79000 you¦79000 discourage¦79000 \add ≈Israeli¦79005 enthusiasm\add* for¦78999 crossing over¦79007 into¦79008 the¦79010 land¦79010 that¦79011 Yahweh¦79015 has¦79013 given¦79013 them¦79014?
\v 8 Your parents did¦79018 that at¦79020 Kadesh¦79022-Barnea when¦79020 I¦79020 sent¦79020 them¦79021 \add in\add* to¦79024 \add ≈survey\add* the¦79027 land.\x + \xo 32:8-9: \xt Num 13:17-33.\x*
\v 9 They¦79029 went¦79029 as far as the Eshkol¦79033 \add ≈valley\add* and¦79029 they saw¦79034 the land, \add ≈yet\add* they discouraged¦79038 the \add ≈people¦79042 from\add* entering the land that¦79050 Yahweh¦79054 had¦79052 given¦79052 them¦79053.
\v 10 Yahweh¦79059 \add ≈got very angry\add* that¦79061 day¦79060, and¦79062 \add ≈promised\add*,
\v 11 ‘From the men¦79068 who came¦79069 out of¦79071 Egypt¦79070, no man who's twenty¦79072 or older will see¦79067 the land which¦79077 I¦79078 promised to Abraham¦79079, Yitshak \add !(Isaac¦79080)\add*, and¦79081 Yakov¦79081 \add !(Jacob¦79081)\add*, because¦79082 they're not¦79083 \add ≈fully with\add* me¦79086.
