\v 28 \add ≈So¦79334\add* Mosheh¦79336 \add ≈gave instructions¦79334\add* about¦79342 them to the priest¦79339 Eleazar¦79338, Nun's¦79344 son¦79342 Yehoshua¦79341, and¦79334 the \add ≈Israeli¦79351 tribal leaders\add*,\x + \xo 32:28-32: \xt Josh 1:12-15.\x*
\v 29 telling them, “If¦79356 the \add ≈men from Gad¦79361 and Reuven¦79364 tribes\add* cross¦79358 over the Yarden¦79369 with¦79366 you \add ≈and equipped¦79372 ready to fight for\add* Yahweh¦79375 and that land \add ≈is conquered\add*, then¦79353 you must¦79358 give¦79379 them the Gilead¦79384 \add ≈region¦79383 for them to own¦79385\add*.
\v 30 \add ≈However,\add* if¦79387 they don't¦79389 cross¦79390 over¦79390 with¦79394 \add the rest of\add* you, then¦79387 \add ≈they'll¦79390 have¦79393 to accept\add* land¦79396 \add ≈to own\add* \add there\add* in¦79394 Kanaan¦79397 \add !(Canaan¦79397)\add*.”
\p
\v 31 “What Yahweh¦79409 has¦79408 told you, \add &his\add* servants¦79412, that's what we'll¦79414 do¦79414,” the \add ≈leaders of the Gad¦79402 and¦79403 Reuven¦79404 tribes responded\add*.
\v 32 We'll¦79416 \add ≈send armed men across\add* to Kanaan¦79422, equipped¦79418 to fight for Yahweh¦79420. \add ≈However,\add* our¦79425 inheritance¦79425 to own¦79424 will¦79423 be¦79423 \add here\add* on this side¦79426 of the¦79426 Yarden¦79427 \add river\add*.”
\p
\v 33 \add ≈So¦79429\add* Mosheh¦79432 gave¦79429 \add <that region\add* to the tribes¦79440 of Reuben¦79437 and Gad¦79435, the half-tribe of Yosef's¦79445 son¦79443 Menashsheh¦79442, \add encompassing\add* the kingdoms¦79448 of the Amorite¦79451 King Sihon¦79449 and the Bashan's¦79457 King Og¦79455, plus¦79436 the surrounding territories¦79460.
