\v 5 After leaving Rameses¦79660, the¦79657 \add ≈Israelis¦79659\add* \add went\add* to Sukkot¦79662 and¦79661 camped¦79661 \add there\add*.
\v 6 Then¦79664 they left¦79664 Sukkit¦79665 and¦79666 camped¦79666 at Etam¦79667 at the edge¦79669 of¦79669 the wilderness¦79670.
\v 7 \add ≈After\add* Etam¦79673, they¦79672 turned¦79674 back¦79674 to¦79675 Pi¦79677-Hahirot (opposite Baal¦79683-Tsefon) and¦79672 camped¦79685 \add ≈facing\add* Migdal.
\v 8 Then¦79689 they¦79689 left¦79689 Pi-Hahirot¦79691 and walked through the middle¦79693 of¦79693 the sea¦79695 into the Etam¦79702 wilderness and camped¦79703 at¦79693 Marah¦79704.
\v 9 From¦79707 Marah¦79707, they went¦79708 to¦79709 Eylim¦79709 which had twelve springs¦79713 with¦79710 seventy¦79715 palm¦79716 trees¦79716 \add around them\add*, and¦79706 they camped¦79717 there¦79719.
\v 10 \add ≈After\add* Eylam, they camped¦79723 beside the¦79726 Red Sea¦79726
\v 11 before leaving the sea¦79731 and camping in the Sin¦79737 wilderness.\f + \fr 33:11 \ft Note that this is located in the southwestern Sinai Peninsula (between Eylim and Mt. Sinai), and different from the Tsin \+add (Zin)\+add* wilderness (which is located in the northern Negev desert, near Kadesh-Barnea).\f*
\v 12 \add ≈Travelling¦79742 from¦79740 there,\add* they¦79743 camped¦79743 at¦79744 Dofkah¦79744,
\v 13 and¦79748 then¦79746 from¦79747 there, at¦79749 Alush¦79749.
\v 14 \add ≈After leaving\add* Alush¦79752, they camped¦79753 at¦79754 Refidim¦79754 \add but\add* they didn't¦79755 have water¦79759 there¦79758 to drink¦79761.
\v 15 \add ≈When¦79763\add* they left¦79763 Refidim¦79764, they camped¦79765 in¦79766 the¦79766 Sinai¦79767 wilderness¦79766.
\s1 The journey legs in the wilderness
\p
\v 16 From¦79770 the¦79770 Sinai¦79771 wilderness¦79770, they¦79772 went to Kivot-Hattaavah and¦79772 camped¦79772 \add there\add*.
\v 17 \add ≈When¦79776\add* they left¦79776 Kivot-Hattaavah, they camped¦79779 at¦79780 Hatserot¦79780,
