\p
\v 50 Then Yahweh¦80024 spoke¦80023 to¦80025 Mosheh¦80027 \add there\add* on¦80028 the Moav¦80029 plains¦80028 beside the Yarden¦80032 \add ≈opposite\add* Yeriho¦80033,
\v 51 “Tell the \add ≈Israelis¦80039\add* that you're all about¦80045 to cross¦80045 the Yahweh to enter Canaan¦80052.
\v 52 Then¦80054 you all must¦80054 \add ≈drive¦80054 all the¦80059 land's¦80060 inhabitants¦80059 out ahead of you\add*, and destroy¦80062 all their carved¦80066 images and cast metal¦80071 images, and all their \add ≈hilltop¦80076 shrines¦80076\add*.
\v 53 Take¦80079 the¦80082 land¦80082 from there and¦80079 start to live there, because¦80086 I've¦80088 given¦80088 \add *it\add* to all of you to own¦80079.
\v 54 \add ≈Use lots\add* to divide the land up for your clans¦80100. \add ≈The larger¦80101 groups must¦80095 get more than the smaller¦80106 groups\add*, then¦80095 \add ≈whatever the lot¦80117 gives, that will¦80119 be the area to be given within the land for that ancestral¦80121 tribe¦80120\add*.\x + \xo 33:54: \xt Num 26:54-56.\x*
\p
\v 55 If¦80124 you don't¦80126 \add ≈drive out the current inhabitants¦80130\add*, then¦80124 they'll become like barbs¦80137 in your eyes¦80138 and thorns¦80139 in your sides¦80140, and they'll harass you all \add ≈when you live there\add*.
\v 56 \add ≈If that happens,\add* then¦80151 I'll¦80156 \add ≈give you all the punishment\add* that I intended¦80153 for¦80154 them¦80155.”
\c 34
