\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦80161 told Mosheh¦80164 \add !(Moses¦80164)\add*,
\v 2 “Tell the \add ≈people¦80170\add* that you're all about¦80177 to enter Canaan¦80181—the land that will become your inheritance¦80187. \add ≈The boundaries¦80190 will be\add*:
\p
\v 3 “The \bd southern¦80196\bd* border will extend from the Tsin¦80199 wilderness¦80197 along the Edom¦80203 border across to the Salt¦80211 \add !(Dead¦80211)\add* Sea¦80209 on the east,
\v 4 cross south of the Scorpion¦80219 Pass¦80220, continue to Tsin¦80221, and go south of Kadesh¦80226-Barnea. Then¦80214 it¦80228 will¦80228 go on to Hatsar¦80229-Addar¦80231 and proceed to Atsmon¦80233,
\v 5 From Atsmon¦80237 \add it will extend west\add* to the riverbed¦80238 at the border¦80236 with Egypt¦80239, and¦80240 then¦80235 across to the \add Mediterranean\add* Sea¦80242.
\p
\v 6 “The \bd western\bd* border¦80255 will¦80253 be¦80253 the¦80256 \add ≈Mediterranean\add* sea¦80248.
\p
\v 7 “The \bd northern¦80263\bd* border¦80262 will start at the \add ≈Mediterranean\add* sea¦80266 and¦80258 extend west to Mt¦80271. Hor¦80270,
\v 8 and then on to Levo¦80276-Hamat¦80277 and onward to Tsedad¦80281.
\v 9 \add From there\add* the border will extend¦80283 to Zifron¦80285, and¦80283 it¦80292 will end at Hatsar¦80288-Eynan¦80289, \add ≈completing\add* the northern¦80295 border.
\p
\v 10 “The \bd eastern¦80300\bd* border¦80299 will begin at Hatsar¦80301-Eynan and¦80297 extend \add south\add* to Shefam¦80303,
\v 11 then go¦80305 downhill to Rivlah¦80308 east of Ayin¦80310, then along the \add ≈hills\add* to the east of Lake Galilee \add (Heb. Kinneret)\add*.
\v 12 Then¦80322 the border¦80323 will¦80325 extend \add south\add* along the Yarden¦80324 \add River\add* and¦80322 \add ≈end¦80326 at\add* the Salt¦80328 \add !(Dead¦80328)\add* Sea¦80327.
\p “Those will be¦80330 your \add ≈country's\add* borders¦80333.”
\p
\v 13 Then¦80336 Mosheh¦80337 \add ≈continued\add*, “That will be the land¦80344 that¦80345 \add must be distributed\add* by lot¦80348. It'll be given¦80352 by Yahweh¦80351 as an inheritance¦80346 for the nine¦80353 tribes¦80354 and¦80336 the Menashsheh half-tribe\x + \xo 34:13: \xt Num 26:52-56.\x*
\v 14 \add as\add* the Reuven¦80362 and Gad¦80368 tribes¦80365 and the Menashsheh¦80373 half-tribe have¦80374 already received their¦80375 inheritance¦80375.
\v 15 \add Yes,\add* the \add other\add* two¦80377 and¦80379 a half¦80379 tribes¦80378 have¦80381 taken¦80381 up their¦80382 inheritance¦80382 on the eastern¦80386 side¦80383 of¦80379 the Yarden¦80384 \add river\add* across from¦80383 Yeriho¦80385 \add !(Jericho¦80385)\add*.
\s1 The teachers egpepamaaren of land
\rem /s1 Tribal Leaders; Leaders to Divide the Land; The Leaders Responsible for Dividing the Land
\p
\v 16 Then Yahweh¦80391 told Mosheh¦80394,
\v 17 “These¦80397 are¦80398 the men¦80399 who¦80400 will¦80402 \add ≈distribute\add* the land¦80406: the priest¦80408 Eleazar¦80407 and¦80409 Nun's¦80412 son¦80410 Yehoshua¦80409 \add !(Joshua¦80409)\add*,
\v 18 as well as one¦80415 leader¦80416 from¦80418 each tribe¦80418 to¦80420 allocate the¦80423 land¦80423 that will be their inheritance¦80420.
\v 19 Those \add tribe\add* leaders are:
\li1 From¦80429 Yehudah¦80429 \add !(Judah¦80429)\add*, Yefunneh's¦80433 son¦80431 Kalev¦80430 \add !(Caleb¦80430)\add*,
\li1
\v 20 From Shimeon¦80437, Ammihud's¦80441 son¦80439 Shemuel¦80438,
\li1
\v 21 From Benyamin¦80444, Kislon's son¦80446 Elidad¦80445,
\li1
\v 22 From Dan¦80453, Yogli's¦80458 son¦80456 Bukki¦80455,
\li1
\v 23 From¦80461 Menashsheh¦80465, Efod's¦80470 son¦80468 Hanniyel¦80467,
\li1
\v 24 From Efrayim¦80475, Shiftan's¦80480 son¦80478 Kemuel¦80477,
\li1
\v 25 From Zevulun¦80485, Parnach's¦80490 son¦80488 Elizafan¦80487,
\li1
\v 26 From Yissakar¦80495, Azzan's¦80500 son¦80498 Paltiel¦80497,
\li1
\v 27 From Asher¦80505, Shelomi's¦80510 son¦80508 Ahihud¦80507,
\li1
\v 28 From Naftali¦80515, Ammihud's¦80520 son¦80518 Pedahel¦80517.”
\p
\v 29 \add ≈The¦80531 above\add* are¦80523 \add the men\add* that Yahweh¦80525 \add ≈put in¦80532 charge of¦80533 dividing up\add* Kanaan¦80533 as¦80526 the inheritance¦80526 for the \add ≈Israelis¦80529\add*.
\c 35
\s1 Cities for the Levites
\rem /s1 Towns for the Levites; The Cities Assigned to the Levites; Cities for the Levites
\p
\v 1 \add ≈While\add* they were there on¦80541 the Moav¦80542 plains¦80541 beside the Yarden¦80545 \add river\add*, Yahweh¦80537 told Mosheh¦80540 \add !(Moses)\add*.\x + \xo 35:1-8: \xt Josh 21:1-42.\x*
\v 2 “Tell the \add Israelis\add* that out of¦80552 the land¦80560 that they'll¦80554 \add ≈own¦80557\add*, they must¦80554 give¦80554 the Levites¦80555 cities for them to live in, \add ≈as well as\add* some pastureland¦80560 around¦80562 \add &those\add* cities.
\v 3 The cities¦80567 will be for them¦80568 to¦80569 live¦80569 in¦80569, and that pastureland¦80570 will be for their herds and their flocks, and for their other animals¦80575.
\v 4 The pastureland¦80577 must¦80580 extend out half a kilometre around¦80587 the walls of¦80582 the Levites¦80581 cities¦80578.
\v 5 Then¦80589 going out a kilometre \add ≈in each compass direction\add*, that will¦80622 also be their land.\f + \fr 35:5 \ft It's not exactly clear what different activities would occur in these two rings of land, but remember that as much food as possible and animals would have to be brought into the city as soon as the residents received news of an approaching army.\f*
\rem /s1 Cities of Refuge
\v 6 The¦80628 Levites¦80631 \add ≈must be given forty-two¦80644 cities to live in, plus¦80642\add* you all must \add ≈designate\add* six¦80633 refuge cities so that¦80629 if someone accidentally kills another, they can flee¦80639 to the refuge city.
\v 7 \add ≈That would make a total of¦80648\add* forty-eight¦80654 cities¦80650, plus¦80655 their¦80660 pasturelands¦80660, to be¦80654 given¦80652 to the Levites¦80653.
\v 8 The¦80662 larger¦80670 tribes must¦80664 give¦80664 more cities¦80681 than the smaller¦80673 tribes, according¦80676 to¦80676 the area that¦80663 they¦80679 inherit¦80677.”
\s1 The refuge cities
\rem /s1 Cities of Refuge; The Cities of Refuge
\r (Deu. 19:1-13; Josh. 20:1-9)
\p
\v 9 Then Yahweh¦80686 told Mosheh¦80689,\x + \xo 35:9-28: \xt Deu 19:2-4; Josh 20:1-9.\x*
\v 10 “Tell¦80696 the \add ≈Israelis¦80695\add* that when you¦80697 cross¦80701 the Yarden¦80704 \add river\add* \add ≈to enter\add* Kanaan¦80706,
\v 11 you all must¦80708 choose some cities to become ‘refuge¦80712 cities’ \add so that\add* if someone accidentally¦80721 kills another person¦80720, they¦80713 can flee¦80715 there¦80716.
\v 12 The cities¦80725 will¦80723 be places to¦80724 stay safe from¦80727 \add ≈being avenged¦80727\add* \add by the relatives\add* until¦80731 the killer¦80730 can \add ≈be formally tried\add*.
\v 13 You all must¦80740 \add ≈allocate\add* six¦80741 refuge¦80744 cities—
\v 14 three¦80750 on the eastern side of¦80754 the Yarden¦80754, and there on the western side in¦80759 Kanann¦80760.
\v 15 Both¦80766 \add ≈Israelis¦80765\add* and \add ≈foreigners living in¦80769 the country\add* can flee¦80776 to¦80776 \add any of\add* those¦80774 six¦80771 cities¦80773—anyone¦80780 who¦80780 kills \add another\add* person¦80782 by¦80783 accident¦80783.
\rem /s1 Concerning Murder and Blood Revenge
\p
\v 16 “However, if¦80785 someone strikes¦80790 \add @another person\add* with¦80787 \add ≈a metal object¦80787\add* and they die¦80794, then¦80785 that person is¦80792 a murderer, and murderers must¦80795 be¦80795 \add ≈executed¦80795\add*.
\v 17 \add ≈Similarly,\add* anyone who strikes¦80805 \add @another person\add* when holding a \add rock or\add* stone¦80799, then¦80798 that¦80801 person is¦80807 a murderer, and¦80798 murderers must¦80803 be¦80810 \add ≈executed¦80810\add*.
\v 18 \add ≈Again,\add* if someone¦80820 strikes¦80822 \add @another person\add* with¦80814 a piece of¦80814 wood¦80815, then that¦80818 person is a murderer, and murderers must¦80820 be¦80827 \add ≈executed¦80827\add*.
\v 19 The \add relative who\add* is avenging¦80830 the \add spilt\add* blood¦80831 must¦80833 \add ≈execute the murderer¦80836 as soon as he finds them\add*.
\p
\v 20 “If¦80843 someone pushes¦80846 \add @another person\add* in hatred¦80845, or¦80847 lies¦80851 in wait¦80851 and¦80852 then¦80843 throws¦80849 something at¦80845 them,
\v 21 or angrily strikes¦80856 them with¦80855 their hand¦80857, and then they die¦80859, \add ≈it¦80858 must be¦80861 regarded as murder,\add* and when the avenger¦80865 of¦80865 their blood¦80866 finds the murderer, he must \add ≈execute\add* them.
\p
\v 22 “\add ≈But¦80875\add* if¦80875 someone pushes¦80881 \add @another person\add* without any hateful \add intent\add*, or throws¦80884 something at¦80877 them without lying¦80890 in¦80877 wait¦80890,
\v 23 or drops a rock¦80895 without \add ≈noticing\add* someone¦80898, and they die¦80898 \add ≈but¦80902\add* they weren't \add @that¦80896 person's\add* enemy¦80908 and no harm¦80912 was intended,
\v 24 then¦80914 the community must¦80914 judge¦80914 between¦80916 the \add ≈one¦80917 who¦80917 killed\add* and¦80918 the avenger¦80919 \add ≈of¦80919 the dead person\add*, in accordance with these¦80923 regulations.
\v 25 \add If the one who killed is declared innocent\add*, then¦80925 the community must rescue¦80925 them from¦80930 the avenger¦80931 and return¦80933 them to the refuge¦80939 city¦80938 that they'd fled¦80942 to, and \add ≈that accidental killer¦80929\add* must live¦80944 there¦80943 until¦80946 after the death¦80948 of¦80948 the high priest¦80949 (who had¦80953 been anointed¦80953 with¦80945 sacred¦80956 oil¦80955).
\v 26 \add ≈However,\add* if¦80958 they then¦80958 ever¦80960 left the refuge¦80967 city¦80966 that they'd fled¦80969 to,
\v 27 and the avenger found¦80972 them outside¦80976 the city¦80978 boundary, then¦80972 \add ≈that relative of the dead person\add* is permitted to kill¦80980 that person and won't¦80986 be accountable for their blood¦80988.
\v 28 \add That's\add* because¦80990 the \add ≈one who killed¦81004\add* must¦80993 remain¦80993 in¦80991 that city¦80991 until¦80994 the death of the high priest—they can only return¦81003 to \add ≈their family home\add* after¦80999 the high priest's death.
\v 29 You all¦81016 must¦81010 \add follow\add* these¦81011 regulations¦81013 through¦81015 the generations¦81015 no matter where you live¦81017.
\p
\v 30 “\add If\add* someone¦81026 murders¦81029 \add another\add* person¦81023, they're to¦81024 be executed if there's evidence¦81024 from witnesses¦81025 (\add plural,\add* not just one witness¦81025).
\v 31 That sentence \add ≈can't¦81038 be changed to a fine and¦81038/or a payment to the deceased's family\add*—\add @the murderer\add* \em must¦81040\em* be executed¦81052.
\v 32 \add ≈Similarly for the accidental killer who fled¦81058 to a refuge¦81062 city¦81061\add*, they can't¦81054 \add ≈elect to pay a fine and¦81054/or pay compensation\add* in order to be able to return¦81063 \add ≈home\add* before the high priest's¦81069 death¦81068.
\v 33 You mustn't profane the land that¦81077 you're all going to \add by tolerating murder\add*, because¦81080 \add human\add* blood pollutes¦81073 the ground, and¦81071 you all can't¦81071 \add ≈restore the land with¦81079 any sacrifice\add*—only by the blood of¦81099 the one¦81100 who¦81100 shed¦81093 \add someone else's\add* blood.
\v 34 You¦81103 mustn't profane the¦81106 land¦81106 that¦81107 you'll¦81103 all be living in because¦81115 I'll also be living in it¦81114, as I will¦81109 live among \add you\add* \add ≈Israelis¦81120\add*.”
\c 36
\s1 Women inheriting property
\rem /s1 Women Who Inherit Property; Marriage of Female Heirs; The Inheritance of Married Women; Inheritance of Zelophehad's Daughters
\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now\add* the leaders of the Gilead clans¦81137 (\add ≡Gilead was\add* the son of Makir¦81133, son of Menashsheh¦81136, one of Yosef's¦81139 sons) approached Mosheh¦81142 and the \add ≈Israeli¦81148\add* leaders
\v 2 and said¦81150, “Yahweh commanded my master to \add ≈distribute\add* the land¦81159 by lot as an inheritance \add ≈for the people¦81162\add*, and my master was¦81165 \add also\add* commanded by Yahweh to give¦81167 our¦81172 brother¦81172 Tselofehad's¦81171 inheritance to his¦81173 daughters¦81173.\x + \xo 36:2: \xt Num 27:7.\x*
\v 3 \add ≈However¦81181, if\add* they¦81175 \add ended up\add* \add ≈being married by men from other\add* tribes, then¦81175 their inheritance would \add ≈pass from our tribe¦81190 to¦81188 their husbands' tribes, so we'd end up with less land as our tribal\add* inheritance.
\v 4 Then¦81198 when Yisrael¦81203 celebrates the Jubilee¦81201 \add Year\add*, then¦81198 that¦81209 inheritance will¦81204 be added¦81204 to¦81206 the inheritance of \add @their husbands'\add* tribes, and¦81198 be deducted from¦81212 the inheritance of our¦81214 \add ≈ancestral¦81214\add* tribe¦81213.”
\p
\v 5 Then¦81218 Mosheh¦81219 \add ≈gave a ruling\add* to¦81228 the \add ≈Israelis¦81222\add* \add ≈in accordance with what Yahweh¦81227 had told¦81218 him\add*, “These \add ≈Yosefite men\add* are correct.
\v 6 Yahweh's¦81241 \add ≈command¦81240\add* to Tselofehad's¦81243 daughters¦81242 is¦81237 that¦81238 \add ≈each of¦81243 you may marry whoever you want as long as it's someone from your own¦81246\add* tribe¦81251.
\v 7 That¦81273 way, land \add ≈in¦81268 Yisrael¦81261\add* won't¦81256 \add ≈move\add* from¦81262 tribe to tribe, because¦81266 \add ≈it¦81258 will always stay as part of¦81268\add* the¦81269 inheritance¦81268 \add ≈given to that\add* tribe.
\v 8 \add ≈Any woman¦81288 who¦81278 inherits¦81279 land can only marry someone from¦81280 her¦81286 own\add* tribe¦81280, so¦81289 that¦81289 the¦81291 people¦81291 will¦81287 \add always\add* \add ≈retain ownership of their tribal\add* inheritance¦81294.
\v 9 \add &That\add* inheritance mustn't pass from¦81301 tribe to¦81302 tribe, but¦81297 each \add ≈Israeli¦81311\add* tribe must¦81299 keep hold¦81308 of¦81307 its¦81307 inheritance.”
\p
\v 10 ⇔So Tselofehad's¦81322 daughters¦81321 obeyed what Yahweh¦81315 had¦81314 told¦81314 Mosheh¦81318,
\v 11 and the \add five\add* daughters¦81330 (Mahlah¦81325, Tirtsah¦81326, Hoglah¦81327, Milkah, and Noah¦81329) married their \add ≈cousins on their father's¦81333 side\add*.
\v 12 \add ≈The men they¦81343 married\add* were from the Menashsheh¦81339 tribe (Yosef's¦81342 son¦81340), so \add ≈their land continued to belong to their father's¦81351 family and¦81345\add* tribe.
\p
\v 13 \add ≈All¦81365 the above\add* were the commands¦81354 and regulations that¦81356 Yahweh¦81358 ordered¦81357 Mosheh¦81361 to¦81362 tell the \add ≈Israelis¦81364\add*, \add while they were camped\add* on¦81359 the Moav¦81367 plains¦81366 beside the Yarden¦81369 \add river\add* \add ≈opposite\add* Yeriho¦81370 \add !(Jericho¦81370)\add*.
